// open-source under the Mozilla Public License 2.0:
//   https://www.tradingview.com/script/0KTDWTdN-ICT-HTF-Candles-Source-Code-fadi/
// Original copyright retained per MPL-2.0. This script is published open-source under the same
// licence, as MPL-2.0 requires of anything derived from it.
//
// Carried over from that script, substantially unchanged: the HTF candle column engine (the Candle,
// CandleSet, Settings, Helper, Trace and Imbalance types, and Monitor, Update, Reorder,
// FindImbalance, DetectSwings, HTFName, RemainingTime, ValidTimeframe, LineStyle, CandleSetHigh/Low,
// CandlesHigh/Low, UpdateTime and HTFEnabled), the HTF swing and equilibrium lines, the fair value
// gap and volume imbalance boxes, the trace lines, the HTF info table, per-chart-timeframe
// visibility, AND the SMT divergence feature itself, including its chart overlay and the Pair 1-8
// correlated-symbol inputs. Full credit for all of that to the original author.
//
// Added here: PSP detection and its glow, Strength Switch, SMTF, SSMT, automatic correlation by
// syminfo.root, three simultaneous correlations with per-correlation toggles, the all-pairs /
// merge / level-break rework of divergence detection, the bundled data-request consolidation, and
// the noise filters.
//
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HTF PSP
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// A multi-timeframe tool for correlated-asset analysis. Up to six higher timeframes are drawn as a
// compact candle column beside price, and two things are marked across them: Precision Swing Points
// and SMT divergence. An analysis aid, not a complete trading system, and nothing here is a signal
// to buy or sell.
//
// PSP (Precision Swing Point) — an HTF candle whose BODY DIRECTION disagrees with a correlated
// asset on the same timeframe: one closes up while the other closes down. The candle takes a
// coloured border plus an optional halo, and a label naming which correlations disagreed and
// whether this symbol is the strong (S) or weak (W) side. A forming candle uses a separate colour,
// because the signal can still invalidate before it closes.
//
// SMT divergence — one asset takes out a prior high or low while its correlated partner fails to.
// Every pair of candles inside a lookback window is tested, so a divergence anchored two or three
// candles back is found, not only the newest pair. Two invalidation rules are enforced per asset:
// the divergence is void if a candle between the endpoints already broke the level being compared,
// and it is finished once a newer candle takes that level. Drawn on the HTF column and, optionally,
// across the actual swing on the chart itself.
//
// SMTF — a divergence whose diverging extreme sits inside a fair value gap that formed BEFORE that
// candle, on either asset. Price delivering into an existing imbalance while the correlation
// cracks. Prefixed "SMTF".
//
// SSMT (sequential SMT) — divergence filtered through TIME. Every cycle divides into four quarters,
// each quarter being one candle of the timeframe below: the monthly cycle into weekly candles, the
// weekly into daily, the daily into four 6H candles (the Asia, London, NY AM and NY PM sessions),
// the session into 90m, the 90m into 22.5m. A divergence between two CONSECUTIVE quarters is
// sequential and is prefixed "SSMT", or "SSMTF" when it also delivered into a gap. Skipping a
// quarter makes it a regular divergence again, whatever the timeframe. Sequential divergences are
// exempt from every display filter, so a decluttering setting can never hide one. Set an HTF slot
// to 6H for session divergence: one index taking the London or Asia low while another fails to.
//
// Strength Switch — divergence filtered through the SWEEP instead: which asset took the prior
// extreme, and which failed to pair it. Four formations, tagged onto the PSP and divergence labels
// already drawn rather than adding marks of their own:
//   SS-SMT             the sweeper shows the higher low / lower high while its counterpart continues
//   SS-SMT two-stage   that, and the SMT's own tip candle is a PSP                        -> "SS²"
//   SS-PSP             a PSP where exactly one asset takes out the lookback extreme
//   SS-PSP two-stage   that, confirmed by a matching-direction SMT on the next pair       -> "SS²"
// Off by default, and each half is independently toggleable: SS-PSP tags candles, SS-SMT tags
// divergence lines, and "Two-stage only" keeps just the SS² form of whichever are on. SS-SMT needs
// only divergence, so it works with PSP highlights off; SS-PSP tags the PSP label and so needs them
// on. Note that SS-SMT and SSMT are different tests despite the similar names: SSMT asks whether the
// two candles are consecutive quarters of a cycle, SS-SMT asks who swept.
//
// Three correlations at once — the original pairs against one correlated symbol; this pairs against
// up to three, all ticked by default, each with its own on/off tick and each dropping out of the
// labels when unticked. On a recognised futures root the symbols are auto-filled, and the leg
// switches at the top of the settings decide which of them get filled at all:
//   NQ / ES     the other index always; then YM (switch, on) and RTY (switch, off)
//   YM          NQ and ES always; then RTY (switch, off)
//   GC / SI     the sibling metal always; then that metal in USD and in EUR (switch, off)
//   CL / HO / RB    the two sibling products
// Anything else falls through to the Pair 1-8 inputs. A blank leg is inactive everywhere and its
// name drops out of every label, so an empty Corr. box is not a fault — it is a leg that is
// switched off, or one this root does not have.
//
// Quick toggles — five shortcuts at the very top of the settings, above everything else:
//   Enable Strength Switch    the master switch for the SS / SS² tags described above
//   Quarterly timeframes      swaps the column onto 30m / 1H / 90m / 4H / 6H, the cycle-quarter
//                             set SSMT keys on. The 15m slot switches off and the daily slot
//                             becomes 6H, which is session divergence. It overrides the timeframe
//                             boxes while ticked, and beats the per-chart-TF visibility rules so
//                             15m cannot come back through the side door.
//   Indices: YM       (on)    pair NQ and ES against the Dow
//   Indices: RTY     (off)    add the Russell as Corr. 3 on NQ, ES and YM
//   Metals: spot FX  (off)    pair GC / SI against XAUUSD + XAUEUR / XAGUSD + XAGEUR as well as
//                             the sibling metal future
// The last three only steer what the auto-fill writes into the Corr. 1-3 boxes on a recognised
// root; on any other chart those boxes are typed by hand and the switches do nothing.
//
// Noise filters — index correlations produce a lot of divergence. "SMT needs every symbol" turns
// the test from ANY correlation to ALL of them, "SMT tips per column" limits how many of the newest
// candles may anchor a line, "Label SMTF lines only" keeps every line but labels only the ones that
// delivered into a gap, and "Merge overlapping chart SMTs" collapses the same swing seen from
// several timeframes down to one line. All default to the busier, unfiltered behaviour.

//@version=6
indicator('HTF PSPˢᵇˢ', overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 5000, calc_bars_count = 5000)

type Candle
	float o
	float c
	float h
	float l
    int o_time
	int o_idx
	int c_idx
	int h_idx
	int l_idx
    string dow
	box body
	line wick_up
	line wick_down
    label dow_label
    line swing_high_line
    line swing_low_line
    line eq_line
    bool has_bearish_div
    bool has_bullish_div
    bool is_psp = false
    label psp_label
    // The merged column SMT this candle is the TIP of — its label and the anchor
    // (older) candle index. Lets DetectStrengthSwitch SS-tag EVERY drawn SMT rather than only one
    // whose tip happens to be the forming candle. Reset each last-bar tick by DetectDivergence.
    label smt_low_lbl
    label smt_high_lbl
    int smt_low_anchor = -1
    int smt_high_anchor = -1

// One row of chart-overlay divergence lines (single high + single low per HTF candle pair, with
// labels showing the combined diverging symbol names — e.g. "SI & USD"). Recreated each bar.
type ChartDivergence
    line  high_line
    line  low_line
    label high_label
    label low_label

// One CANDIDATE chart-overlay SMT. Every HTF collects its overlay SMTs here first;
// nothing is drawn until all six have reported, so overlapping lines from different timeframes can
// be resolved in a single pass (highest timeframe wins).
type ChartSMTCand
    bool   isHigh
    int    xOld
    float  yOld
    int    xNew
    float  yNew
    string txt
    int    tfSecs
    bool   isSmtf
    bool   isSsmt

// One drawn column SMT (a line between a newer candle and an older one, plus its
// optional symbol-name label). Held in a global pool that is cleared and rebuilt every last-bar
// tick, so there is no per-candle persistence bookkeeping (stateless).
type ColumnSMT
    line  ln
    label lbl

type Trace
	line o
	line c
	line h
	line l
	label o_l
	label c_l
	label h_l
	label l_l

type Imbalance
	box b
	int idx

type CandleSettings
	bool show
	string htf
	int max_display

type Settings
	int max_sets
	color bull_body
	color bull_border
	color bull_wick
	color bear_body
	color bear_border
	color bear_wick
	int offset
	int buffer
	int htf_buffer
	int width
	bool use_custom_daily
    string custom_daily
    bool daily_name
	bool trace_show
	color trace_o_color
	string trace_o_style
	int trace_o_size
	color trace_c_color
	string trace_c_style
	int trace_c_size
	color trace_h_color
	string trace_h_style
	int trace_h_size
	color trace_l_color
	string trace_l_style
	int trace_l_size
	string trace_anchor
	bool label_show
	color label_color
	string label_size
    string label_position
    string label_alignment
	bool fvg_show
	color fvg_color
	bool vi_show
	color vi_color
	bool htf_label_show
	color htf_label_color
	string htf_label_size
	bool htf_timer_show
	color htf_timer_color
	string htf_timer_size
    color dow_color
    string dow_size

type CandleSet
	array<Candle> candles
	array<Imbalance> imbalances
	// Chart symbol's own HTF highs/lows, 6 deep, independent of how many candles the column
	// DISPLAYS. The Candle array is capped by max_display (3 on most HTFs), which left the
	// chart-side gap test with nothing to look at; these carry the same depth the correlated
	// symbols get from their bundled security calls, at no extra security cost. Index 0 is the
	// forming candle and is refreshed every chart bar in Update().
	array<float> hHist
	array<float> lHist
	CandleSettings settings
	label tfNameTop
    label tfNameBottom
	label tfTimerTop
    label tfTimerBottom

type Helper
	string name = 'Helper'
	// Per-HTF "visible × valid-timeframe" cache + the HTFEnabled count
	// live as fields on Helper so methods (which can't reference top-level primitive vars in
	// Pine v6) can read them through the `helper` parameter. Populated once on barstate.isfirst.
	bool htf1_active = false
	bool htf2_active = false
	bool htf3_active = false
	bool htf4_active = false
	bool htf5_active = false
	bool htf6_active = false
	int  htf_enabled_count = 0

Settings settings = Settings.new()

var CandleSettings SettingsHTF1 = CandleSettings.new()
var CandleSettings SettingsHTF2 = CandleSettings.new()
var CandleSettings SettingsHTF3 = CandleSettings.new()
var CandleSettings SettingsHTF4 = CandleSettings.new()
var CandleSettings SettingsHTF5 = CandleSettings.new()
var CandleSettings SettingsHTF6 = CandleSettings.new()

var array<Candle> candles_1 = array.new<Candle>(0)
var array<Candle> candles_2 = array.new<Candle>(0)
var array<Candle> candles_3 = array.new<Candle>(0)
var array<Candle> candles_4 = array.new<Candle>(0)
var array<Candle> candles_5 = array.new<Candle>(0)
var array<Candle> candles_6 = array.new<Candle>(0)

var array<Imbalance> imbalances_1 = array.new<Imbalance>()
var array<Imbalance> imbalances_2 = array.new<Imbalance>()
var array<Imbalance> imbalances_3 = array.new<Imbalance>()
var array<Imbalance> imbalances_4 = array.new<Imbalance>()
var array<Imbalance> imbalances_5 = array.new<Imbalance>()
var array<Imbalance> imbalances_6 = array.new<Imbalance>()

var array<float> hhist_1 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_1 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hhist_2 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_2 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hhist_3 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_3 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hhist_4 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_4 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hhist_5 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_5 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> hhist_6 = array.new<float>()
var array<float> lhist_6 = array.new<float>()

var array<ChartDivergence> chart_divs = array.new<ChartDivergence>()
var array<ChartSMTCand> chart_cands = array.new<ChartSMTCand>()
var array<ColumnSMT> col_smts = array.new<ColumnSMT>()
// PSP glow — stateless, cleared and rebuilt each last-bar tick like col_smts. Body rings are
// boxes; the wick backing is lines, so the two pools are separate.
var array<box> psp_glows = array.new<box>()
var array<line> psp_glow_wicks = array.new<line>()

var CandleSet htf1 = CandleSet.new()
htf1.settings := SettingsHTF1
htf1.candles := candles_1
htf1.imbalances := imbalances_1
htf1.hHist := hhist_1
htf1.lHist := lhist_1

var CandleSet htf2 = CandleSet.new()
htf2.settings := SettingsHTF2
htf2.candles := candles_2
htf2.imbalances := imbalances_2
htf2.hHist := hhist_2
htf2.lHist := lhist_2

var CandleSet htf3 = CandleSet.new()
htf3.settings := SettingsHTF3
htf3.candles := candles_3
htf3.imbalances := imbalances_3
htf3.hHist := hhist_3
htf3.lHist := lhist_3

var CandleSet htf4 = CandleSet.new()
htf4.settings := SettingsHTF4
htf4.candles := candles_4
htf4.imbalances := imbalances_4
htf4.hHist := hhist_4
htf4.lHist := lhist_4

var CandleSet htf5 = CandleSet.new()
htf5.settings := SettingsHTF5
htf5.candles := candles_5
htf5.imbalances := imbalances_5
htf5.hHist := hhist_5
htf5.lHist := lhist_5

var CandleSet htf6 = CandleSet.new()
htf6.settings := SettingsHTF6
htf6.candles := candles_6
htf6.imbalances := imbalances_6
htf6.hHist := hhist_6
htf6.lHist := lhist_6

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Settings                                                                                             ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

// Quick toggles. Declared before every other input and left ungrouped, which is what puts them at
// the TOP of the settings panel — TradingView renders inputs in declaration order, ungrouped first.
// Every one of them is a shortcut onto behaviour that also exists further down — the SS master
// switch, the slot-6 timeframe, and which symbols the auto-correlation fills in. None is a
// separate feature, and none of them does anything a user could not do from the groups below.
show_ss                         = input.bool(false, 'Enable Strength Switch', tooltip="Master switch for Strength Switch — the SS / SS² tags on PSP candles and divergence lines. Off by default because it costs six extra data requests while on. WHICH of the four formations get marked is set in the Strength Switch group further down; this turns the whole thing on or off.")
qt_quarterly                    = input.bool(false, 'Quarterly timeframes (90m + 6H)', tooltip="Switches the HTF column onto the CYCLE-QUARTER timeframes, which are the ones SSMT keys on: 30m / 1H / 90m / 4H / 6H. The 15m slot is switched off and the daily slot becomes 6H — the four sessions (Asia, London, NY AM, NY PM) ARE the four quarters of the day, so a 6H column gives session divergence. 90m is already in slot 4 and stays. Overrides the timeframe boxes below while ticked; untick to get them back.")

// Auto-fill leg switches. These decide which symbols the recognised-root auto-correlation below
// puts in the Corr. 1-3 boxes; on an unrecognised chart the boxes are yours and these do nothing.
// A leg switched off is BLANKED rather than merely unticked, and a blank leg is inactive
// everywhere — PSP, both divergence detectors and Strength Switch — so its name also drops out of
// every label.
qt_ym                           = input.bool(true, 'Indices: pair against YM', tooltip="Auto-fill switch: pair NQ and ES against YM. ON by default — the Dow is the classic third leg of the index correlation and it is where a good share of index SMT comes from. Untick to run NQ against ES alone (plus RTY, if that is on). Affects the NQ and ES roots only: on a YM chart YM is the chart symbol, so this does nothing there.")
qt_rty                          = input.bool(false, 'Indices: pair against RTY', tooltip="Auto-fill switch: add RTY to the index correlation — it takes Corr. 3 on NQ and ES, and on YM. OFF by default: the Russell breaks with the big three often enough that it prints a lot of extra lines, which is a useful breadth read and a noisy signal. Affects the NQ, ES and YM roots only.")
qt_metals_fx                    = input.bool(false, 'Metals: pair against spot FX', tooltip="Auto-fill switch: pair GC and SI against the SPOT metal as well as the sibling future — XAUUSD and XAUEUR on gold, XAGUSD and XAGEUR on silver. OFF by default, so a metals chart runs on the futures leg alone (GC against SI). Tick it for the spot legs, which add a currency read: gold diverging against XAUEUR but not XAUUSD is a euro story rather than a gold one. Affects the GC and SI roots only. If USD / EUR never appear in the labels, your data plan cannot resolve the FOREXCOM feed — an unresolvable symbol fails silently by design.")

string group_style              = "Styling  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
string group_label              = "Label Settings  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
string group_imbalance          = "Imbalance  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
string group_trace              = "Trace  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"

htf1.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 1      ', inline = 'htf1') and not qt_quarterly
htf_1                           = input.timeframe('15', '', inline = 'htf1')
htf1.settings.htf := htf_1
htf1.settings.max_display       := input.int(4, '', inline = 'htf1')

htf2.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 2      ', inline = 'htf2')
htf_2                           = input.timeframe('30', '', inline = 'htf2')
htf2.settings.htf := htf_2
htf2.settings.max_display       := input.int(4, '', inline = 'htf2')

htf3.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 3      ', inline = 'htf3')
htf_3                           = input.timeframe('60', '', inline = 'htf3')
htf3.settings.htf := htf_3
htf3.settings.max_display       := input.int(3, '', inline = 'htf3')

htf4.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 4      ', inline = 'htf4')
htf_4                           = input.timeframe('90', '', inline = 'htf4')
htf4.settings.htf               := htf_4
htf4.settings.max_display       := input.int(3, '', inline = 'htf4')

htf5.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 5      ', inline = 'htf5')
htf_5                           = input.timeframe('240', '', inline = 'htf5')
htf5.settings.htf := htf_5
htf5.settings.max_display       := input.int(3, '', inline = 'htf5')

htf6.settings.show              := input.bool(true, 'HTF 6      ', inline = 'htf6')
htf_6_in                        = input.timeframe('1D', '', inline = 'htf6')
// The effective slot-6 timeframe. Everything downstream — the column, the security calls, the
// rollover detection and the custom-daily override — reads htf_6, so swapping it here is enough.
htf_6                           = qt_quarterly ? '360' : htf_6_in
htf6.settings.htf               := htf_6
htf6.settings.max_display       := input.int(3, '', inline = 'htf6')

settings.max_sets               := input.int(6, 'Limit to next HTFs only', minval = 1, maxval = 6)

//+--- Per-Timeframe Visibility Settings ---+//
string group_tf_visibility = "Timeframe Visibility  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"

// Chart TF 1: Enable, Timeframe, then which HTFs show on this TF
tf1_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1', tooltip="Enable visibility control for this chart timeframe")
tf_slot_1 = input.timeframe('30S', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf1 = input.bool(true, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf2 = input.bool(true, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf3 = input.bool(true, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf4 = input.bool(true, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf5 = input.bool(true, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')
tf1_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf1')

// Chart TF 2
tf2_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf_slot_2 = input.timeframe('3', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf1 = input.bool(true, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf2 = input.bool(true, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf3 = input.bool(true, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf4 = input.bool(true, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf5 = input.bool(true, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')
tf2_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf2')

// Chart TF 3
tf3_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf_slot_3 = input.timeframe('5', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf1 = input.bool(true, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf2 = input.bool(true, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf3 = input.bool(true, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf4 = input.bool(true, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf5 = input.bool(true, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')
tf3_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf3')

// Chart TF 4
tf4_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf_slot_4 = input.timeframe('30', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf1 = input.bool(false, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf2 = input.bool(false, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf3 = input.bool(true, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf4 = input.bool(true, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf5 = input.bool(true, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')
tf4_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf4')

// Chart TF 5
tf5_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf_slot_5 = input.timeframe('60', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf1 = input.bool(false, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf2 = input.bool(false, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf3 = input.bool(false, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf4 = input.bool(true, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf5 = input.bool(true, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')
tf5_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf5')

// Chart TF 6
tf6_enabled = input.bool(false, 'TF 6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf_slot_6 = input.timeframe('240', '', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf1 = input.bool(false, '1', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf2 = input.bool(false, '2', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf3 = input.bool(false, '3', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf4 = input.bool(false, '4', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf5 = input.bool(false, '5', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')
tf6_htf6 = input.bool(true, '6', group=group_tf_visibility, inline='tf6')

// Helper function to check if HTF should be visible on current chart timeframe
// When on a configured TF, this OVERRIDES the main HTF enable setting
// defaultShow = the main htf.settings.show value (used when not on a configured TF)
isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(int htfNum, bool defaultShow) =>
    string currentTF = timeframe.period
    
    // Check if current TF matches any enabled visibility slot
    bool on_tf1 = tf1_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_1
    bool on_tf2 = tf2_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_2
    bool on_tf3 = tf3_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_3
    bool on_tf4 = tf4_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_4
    bool on_tf5 = tf5_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_5
    bool on_tf6 = tf6_enabled and currentTF == tf_slot_6
    
    bool visible = defaultShow  // Default to main HTF setting
    
    // If we're on any of the configured TFs, OVERRIDE with that config (ignores main HTF enable)
    if on_tf1 or on_tf2 or on_tf3 or on_tf4 or on_tf5 or on_tf6
        if htfNum == 1
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf1) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf1) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf1) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf1) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf1) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf1)
        else if htfNum == 2
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf2) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf2) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf2) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf2) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf2) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf2)
        else if htfNum == 3
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf3) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf3) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf3) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf3) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf3) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf3)
        else if htfNum == 4
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf4) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf4) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf4) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf4) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf4) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf4)
        else if htfNum == 5
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf5) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf5) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf5) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf5) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf5) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf5)
        else if htfNum == 6
            visible := (on_tf1 and tf1_htf6) or (on_tf2 and tf2_htf6) or (on_tf3 and tf3_htf6) or (on_tf4 and tf4_htf6) or (on_tf5 and tf5_htf6) or (on_tf6 and tf6_htf6)
    
    visible

