// Symbol-name label drawn at the midpoint of each divergence line (e.g. "SI", "SI & USD").
div_label_show = input.bool(true, title="Show Divergence Symbol Labels", group=group_div, tooltip="Print the diverging symbol name(s) on each divergence line. When multiple PSP correlations diverge for the same candle, names are joined with ' & '.")
div_label_color = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0), title="Label Color", group=group_div, inline="div_lbl")
div_label_size  = input.string(size.tiny, title="", options=[size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large], group=group_div, inline="div_lbl")
div_label_smtf_only = input.bool(false, "Label SMTF lines only", group=group_div, tooltip="Print the symbol-name label only on SMTF divergences; plain SMTs still draw their line but go unlabelled. The fastest way to cut label clutter without losing any divergence — the lines are still all there, only the ones that matter announce themselves. SSMT lines, when Flag SSMT is on, are exempt and stay labelled. Needs \"Flag SMTF\" on for the gap half of the test.")
// All-pairs SMT — each displayed candle is tested against every candle up to
// `div_lookback` back, and every diverging pair draws its own line (C0-C1, C0-C2, C1-C2, …).
div_lookback    = input.int(4, "SMT lookback (candles)", minval=1, maxval=6, group=group_div, tooltip="How many candles back each HTF candle is paired against for SMT. EVERY diverging pair within this range draws its own line — e.g. current vs 1-back, current vs 2-back, AND 1-back vs 2-back are all independent SMTs. 1 = adjacent candle only. Capped at 6 by the correlated-symbol data depth; lines only draw to candles the column is displaying, so raise the HTF's candle-display count to see deeper pairs.")
div_require_all = input.bool(false, "SMT needs every symbol", group=group_div, tooltip="OFF (default): ANY enabled correlation diverging draws an SMT — with three correlations on, that is three chances to print a line on every candle pair, which is where most of the clutter comes from. ON: every ENABLED correlation must diverge on the same pair before a line is drawn. A far stricter and much quieter signal; on index correlations it typically removes most of the lines. Applies to the HTF columns and the chart overlay alike.")
div_max_tips    = input.int(5, "SMT tips per column", minval=1, maxval=5, group=group_div, tooltip="How many of the newest candles in a column may anchor (be the newer end of) an SMT. 5 = every candle that can, which is the busiest setting. 1 = only the currently forming candle anchors SMTs, so each column shows at most one low and one high line. This trims which divergences DRAW; it does not change how they are detected. SSMT is EXEMPT — with Flag SSMT on, a sequential divergence always draws whatever this is set to.")
div_chart_merge = input.bool(true, "Merge overlapping chart SMTs", group=group_div, tooltip="ON (default): on the CHART overlay only, when SMT lines from different HTF columns cover the same swing, draw just one, ranked SSMTF then SSMT then SMTF then plain, and only then by highest timeframe and then widest span, so a sequential SMT cannot be hidden by a higher-timeframe regular one. The SSMT ranks apply only while Flag SSMT is on; with it off the order is SMTF then timeframe then span. A 15m, 30m and 1H divergence sitting on the same high collapses to the 1H line. OFF: draw every HTF's overlay SMT, which is what produces stacked near-identical lines. Does not affect the HTF columns.")
show_smtf       = input.bool(true, "Flag SMTF", group=group_div, inline="smt_flags", tooltip="SMTF = an SMT that delivered INTO a gap. An SMT where at least ONE of the two assets has its diverging extreme sitting inside a fair value gap on that same asset qualifies, and its divergence label is prefixed \"SMTF\". Only one side needs to be in a gap. The gap must have formed BEFORE the diverging candle — one the candle itself helps create does not count, since the point is that price delivered into an EXISTING imbalance. Only symbols that actually diverged are tested. The flag is applied to BOTH the HTF column label and the matching chart-overlay label, and an SMTF beats a plain SMT in the overlay merge so a higher timeframe cannot hide it. Every asset — the chart symbol included — is checked against 6 candles of its own HTF history, so this does not depend on how many candles a column displays, and it is evaluated on the DEVELOPING HTF candle from the moment that candle opens rather than at its close. Untick to treat every divergence as a plain SMT.")
show_ssmt       = input.bool(true, "Flag SSMT", group=group_div, inline="smt_flags", tooltip="SSMT = SEQUENTIAL SMT, the time-filtered version: a divergence between two CONSECUTIVE quarters of a cycle. Every cycle divides into four quarters and each quarter is one candle of the timeframe below — monthly into 1W, weekly into 1D, daily into 6H (the four sessions Asia / London / NY AM / NY PM), session into 90m, 90m into 22.5m. Only those five timeframes can produce one, and only on an ADJACENT candle pair: skipping a quarter makes it a regular SMT again, whatever the timeframe. Labelled \"SSMT\", or \"SSMTF\" when it also delivered into a gap (needs Flag SMTF on for that half). An SSMT is EXEMPT from every display filter — the tip cap, the label filter and the overlay merge all let it through, and it outranks a plain higher-timeframe SMT covering the same swing, so nothing can hide one. ON by default. Note the exemption means SSMT lines always draw, whatever the noise filters are set to — that is the point of the flag. Not to be confused with Strength Switch's SS-SMT, which is a different test: SSMT filters on TIME (consecutive quarters), SS-SMT on SWEEP (who took the extreme).")
div_merge       = input.bool(true, "Merge SMTs (one per side)", group=group_div, tooltip="ON (default): per HTF column draw only ONE low and ONE high SMT — the most-recent diverging candle (tip) anchored to the FURTHEST candle it diverges with. As a newer low/high prints it becomes the tip and the older overlapping SMTs merge into that single line — far less clutter. OFF: draw every diverging pair individually (all-pairs; very busy on index correlations).")

// Determine correlated symbol based on enabled pairs.
// syminfo.tickerid + the Pair 1-8 inputs are constants for the script run,
// so the resolution runs once on barstate.isfirst and the results persist via `var`.
var string current_symbol = syminfo.tickerid
var string correlated_symbol = ""

if barstate.isfirst
    // Check each pair in order
    if enable_pair1 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(str.replace_all(pair1_sym1, "CME_MINI:", ""), "CBOT_MINI:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair1_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(str.replace_all(pair1_sym2, "CME_MINI:", ""), "CBOT_MINI:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair1_sym1

    if enable_pair2 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair2_sym1, "COMEX:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair2_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair2_sym2, "COMEX:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair2_sym1

    if enable_pair3 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair3_sym1, "BYBIT:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair3_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair3_sym2, "BYBIT:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair3_sym1

    if enable_pair4 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(str.replace_all(pair4_sym1, "CME_MINI:", ""), "CBOT_MINI:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair4_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(str.replace_all(pair4_sym2, "CME_MINI:", ""), "CBOT_MINI:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair4_sym1

    if enable_pair5 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair5_sym1, "NYMEX:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair5_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair5_sym2, "NYMEX:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair5_sym1

    if enable_pair6 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair6_sym1, "FX_IDC:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair6_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair6_sym2, "FX_IDC:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair6_sym1

    if enable_pair7 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair7_sym1, "NASDAQ:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair7_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair7_sym2, "NASDAQ:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair7_sym1

    if enable_pair8 and correlated_symbol == ""
        if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair8_sym1, "NASDAQ:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair8_sym2
        else if str.contains(current_symbol, str.replace_all(pair8_sym2, "NASDAQ:", ""))
            correlated_symbol := pair8_sym1

//+--- PSP Settings ---+//
string group_psp = "PSP (Precision Swing Points)  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"

show_psp           = input.bool(true, "Show PSP Highlights", group=group_psp, tooltip="A PSP occurs when this symbol's HTF candle body direction (bull/bear) diverges from a correlated asset on the same timeframe — one closes up while the other closes down. The candle keeps its normal fill and takes a coloured BORDER plus an optional halo: the Confirmed colour once the candle has closed, the Developing colour while it is still forming and can invalidate. The label names which correlations disagreed and whether this symbol is the strong (S) or weak (W) side.")
// Each correlation has its own on/off tick. Untick one and it is ignored everywhere — PSP, the
// HTF column SMTs and the chart overlay — so its name also drops out of every label.
psp_use1           = input.bool(true, "Corr. 1", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym1", tooltip="Use this correlation. All three are ticked by default, but WHAT they contain depends on the chart: on a recognised futures root the symbols are auto-filled, and the leg switches at the top of these settings decide which legs get filled at all — YM on the index roots (on), RTY on the index roots (off), the spot metals on GC / SI (off). A leg whose box is empty is inactive everywhere and its name drops out of every label, so an empty box means a leg that is switched off or one this root does not have, not a fault. Untick 1 and 2 to work against the third symbol alone.")
psp_sym1           = input.symbol("CME_MINI:ES1!", "", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym1")
psp_use2           = input.bool(true, "Corr. 2", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym2")
psp_sym2           = input.symbol("CBOT_MINI:YM1!", "", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym2")
psp_use3           = input.bool(true, "Corr. 3", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym3")
psp_sym3           = input.symbol("", "", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym3", tooltip="Third correlated symbol. On a recognised root it is auto-filled, and which symbol lands here is set by the leg switches at the top: RTY on NQ, ES and YM when \"Indices: pair against RTY\" is on, and the EUR-quoted spot metal (XAUEUR / XAGEUR) on GC / SI when \"Metals: pair against spot FX\" is on. Blank otherwise, and a blank symbol is inactive — so leaving Corr. 3 ticked on a chart that does not fill it changes nothing. Type a symbol here to use a third correlation on an unrecognised chart.")
psp_require_both   = input.bool(false, "Require all", group=group_psp, inline="psp_sym2", tooltip="When enabled, ALL enabled correlated symbols must diverge from the chart symbol. When disabled, ANY enabled symbol diverging triggers a PSP.")
psp_border_color   = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0), "Border (Confirmed)", group=group_psp, inline="psp_col")
// Forming-candle PSPs are still developing and can invalidate before close.
psp_dev_border_color = input.color(color.new(color.orange, 0), "Border (Developing)", group=group_psp, inline="psp_col2", tooltip="Border color for a PSP on the currently forming HTF candle — the signal is still developing and can invalidate before the candle closes. Confirmed (closed) PSPs use the Confirmed border color.")
// Thin halo around the whole PSP candle, high to low so it wraps the wicks as well as the body.
psp_glow_show      = input.bool(true, "Glow", group=group_psp, inline="psp_glow", tooltip="Draws a halo around the PSP candle body, with a wider faded line sitting behind each wick — it follows the candle shape rather than boxing in the whole high-to-low range. It takes the candle's own border colour, so confirmed PSPs glow in the Confirmed colour and developing ones in the Developing colour.")
psp_glow_layers    = input.int(2, "Layers", minval=1, maxval=4, group=group_psp, inline="psp_glow", tooltip="How many halo rings to stack. Ring N is N pixels wide, so 2 gives a 1px ring with a fainter 2px one behind it, and the wick backing is one step wider again so the wick itself still reads. The column candles are only a couple of bars wide, so anything above 3 reads as a solid block rather than a glow.")
psp_glow_fade      = input.int(70, "Fade", minval=0, maxval=95, group=group_psp, inline="psp_glow", tooltip="Transparency of the innermost ring, 0 = solid. Each outer ring fades further toward invisible. Higher = subtler.")
psp_label_show     = input.bool(true, "PSP Label", group=group_psp, inline="psp_lbl")
psp_label_color    = input.color(color.new(color.red, 0), "", group=group_psp, inline="psp_lbl")
psp_label_size     = input.string(size.tiny, "", options=[size.tiny, size.small, size.normal, size.large, size.huge], group=group_psp, inline="psp_lbl")

//+--- Strength Switch Settings ---+//
string group_ss = "Strength Switch  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"

// Which of the four formations to mark. SS-PSP and SS-SMT are independent; "Two-stage only" then
// keeps just the confirmed (SS²) form of whichever are on.
ss_show_psp     = input.bool(true, "SS-PSP", group=group_ss, inline="ss_types", tooltip="Mark SS-PSP: a PSP where exactly one asset takes out the lookback extreme and the other fails to pair it. The candle border switches to the SS colour and its PSP label is prefixed. Needs 'Show PSP Highlights' on, since it tags the PSP label. Untick to leave PSP candles alone and use Strength Switch on divergence lines only.")
ss_show_smt     = input.bool(true, "SS-SMT", group=group_ss, inline="ss_types", tooltip="Mark SS-SMT: a divergence where the asset that swept the prior extreme is the one showing the higher low / lower high, while its counterpart carries on. Prefixed onto the divergence label. Works with 'Show PSP Highlights' off — this one only needs divergence. Merge mode only, since it reads the merged line each candle anchors.")
ss_two_stage_only = input.bool(false, "Two-stage only (SS²)", group=group_ss, inline="ss_types", tooltip="Keep only the CONFIRMED form of each: an SS-SMT whose own tip candle is also a PSP, or an SS-PSP followed by a matching-direction divergence on the next candle pair. Both print as SS². Much rarer and much quieter. Note this also hides the developing candle's SS-PSP entirely — its confirming divergence would form on the next candle pair, which does not exist yet, so it can never be two-stage.")
ss_border_color = input.color(color.new(#00BCD4, 0), "SS-PSP Border", group=group_ss, inline="ss_col", tooltip="Border color for SS-PSP candles. Takes precedence over the Developing/Confirmed PSP border colors.")
// The order-paired extreme can sit 1-2 candles back, not only on the adjacent candle.
ss_lookback     = input.int(4, "Sweep lookback (candles)", minval=1, maxval=4, group=group_ss, tooltip="How many prior HTF candles form the reference extreme for sweep / failure-to-pair tests. The order-paired level is the highest high / lowest low across that window. 4 (default) = previous four candles; 1 = strictly the previous candle.")
ss_require_reversal = input.bool(false, "Require reversal close (strict)", group=group_ss, tooltip="When ON, an SS-PSP additionally requires the sweeping asset to close AGAINST its sweep (bearish close after taking a high / bullish close after taking a low) — the textbook reversal flavor only. When OFF (default), the catch-up flavor also qualifies: any PSP where exactly one asset takes out the lookback extreme and the other fails to pair it.")

//+--- HTF Info Table Settings ---+//
string group_table = "HTF Info Table  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"

show_htf_table = input.bool(false, title="Show HTF Info Table", group=group_table)
table_position = input.string("Top Right", title="Position", options=["Middle Right", "Top Right", "Bottom Right"], group=group_table)
table_size = input.string("Small", title="Size", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal"], group=group_table)

// Table styling
table_header_bg = input.color(color.new(color.white, 0), title="Header", group=group_table, inline="header_style")
table_header_text = input.color(color.black, title="Text", group=group_table, inline="header_style")
table_label_bg = input.color(color.new(color.white, 20), title="Label", group=group_table, inline="label_style")
table_label_text = input.color(color.black, title="Text", group=group_table, inline="label_style")
table_cell_bg = input.color(color.new(color.white, 30), title="Cell", group=group_table, inline="cell_style")
table_cell_text = input.color(color.black, title="Text", group=group_table, inline="cell_style")

show_timeframe_row = input.bool(true, title="Timeframe", group=group_table, inline="rows1")
show_timer_row = input.bool(true, title="Time to Close", group=group_table, inline="rows1")
show_swing_row = input.bool(true, title="Active Swing", group=group_table, inline="rows2")
show_expansion_row = input.bool(true, title="Expansion", group=group_table, inline="rows2")
show_divergence_row = input.bool(true, title="Divergence", group=group_table, inline="rows3")

// Convert swing settings
confirmed_swing_style_value = confirmed_swing_style == "Solid" ? line.style_solid : confirmed_swing_style == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted
potential_swing_style_value = potential_swing_style == "Solid" ? line.style_solid : potential_swing_style == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted
eq_line_style_value = eq_line_style_input == "Solid" ? line.style_solid : eq_line_style_input == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted
div_line_style_value = div_line_style == "Solid" ? line.style_solid : div_line_style == "Dashed" ? line.style_dashed : line.style_dotted

// Convert table settings
table_size_value = table_size == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : table_size == "Small" ? size.small : size.normal
table_position_value = table_position == "Middle Right" ? position.middle_right : table_position == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : position.bottom_right

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Variables                                                                                            ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Auto-correlation override (indices + metals + oils)                                                  ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
// Effective symbols = user inputs by default; overridden when chart matches a known root.
//
// switched from str.contains(syminfo.ticker, "NQ") substring matching to exact-root
// matching via syminfo.root. The v3 substring approach mis-fired on unrelated tickers like ESLT
// (Elbit Systems contains "ES"), MSFT contains "S", CLF (Cleveland-Cliffs contains "CL"), RBLX,
// etc. — silently overriding the user's correlation with the wrong futures pair.
//
// syminfo.root returns the root symbol for futures (e.g. "NQ" for NQ1!/NQH2024/MNQ1!) and the
// full ticker for non-futures. Exact equality + explicit micro-root entries make every match
// intentional. Unrecognized symbols fall through to the user's Pair-based inputs.
// all of these depend only on syminfo.root / syminfo.ticker and the PSP
// inputs, all of which are constants for the script run. Hoisted into `var` + barstate.isfirst
// so the 8-branch if-else chain runs once instead of every bar.
var string _chart_root   = syminfo.root
var string psp_sym1_eff = psp_sym1
var string psp_sym2_eff = psp_sym2
var string psp_sym3_eff = psp_sym3
var bool _psp_auto_active = false
var bool psp_sym1_enabled = false
var bool psp_sym2_enabled = false
var bool psp_sym3_enabled = false
if barstate.isfirst
    // Indices (NQ / ES / YM — including micro contracts)
    if _chart_root == "NQ" or _chart_root == "MNQ"
        psp_sym1_eff := "CME_MINI:ES1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := qt_ym ? "CBOT_MINI:YM1!" : ""
        psp_sym3_eff := qt_rty ? "CME_MINI:RTY1!" : ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    else if _chart_root == "ES" or _chart_root == "MES"
        psp_sym1_eff := "CME_MINI:NQ1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := qt_ym ? "CBOT_MINI:YM1!" : ""
        psp_sym3_eff := qt_rty ? "CME_MINI:RTY1!" : ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    else if _chart_root == "YM" or _chart_root == "MYM"
        psp_sym1_eff := "CME_MINI:NQ1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := "CME_MINI:ES1!"
        psp_sym3_eff := qt_rty ? "CME_MINI:RTY1!" : ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    // Metals (GC / SI — including micro contracts)
    else if _chart_root == "GC" or _chart_root == "MGC"
        psp_sym1_eff := "COMEX:SI1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := qt_metals_fx ? "FOREXCOM:XAUUSD" : ""
        psp_sym3_eff := qt_metals_fx ? "FOREXCOM:XAUEUR" : ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    else if _chart_root == "SI" or _chart_root == "SIL"
        psp_sym1_eff := "COMEX:GC1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := qt_metals_fx ? "FOREXCOM:XAGUSD" : ""
        psp_sym3_eff := qt_metals_fx ? "FOREXCOM:XAGEUR" : ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    // Oils (CL / HO / RB — including micro WTI)
    else if _chart_root == "CL" or _chart_root == "MCL"
        psp_sym1_eff := "NYMEX:HO1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := "NYMEX:RB1!"
        psp_sym3_eff := ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    else if _chart_root == "HO"
        psp_sym1_eff := "NYMEX:CL1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := "NYMEX:RB1!"
        psp_sym3_eff := ""
        _psp_auto_active := true
    else if _chart_root == "RB"
        psp_sym1_eff := "NYMEX:CL1!"
        psp_sym2_eff := "NYMEX:HO1!"
        psp_sym3_eff := ""
        _psp_auto_active := true

    // Mirror PSP auto-correlation into the divergence detector. On recognized charts the divergence
    // overlay pairs against the same primary symbol as PSP (psp_sym1_eff), overriding any match the
    // Pair 1-8 inputs may have produced earlier. Unrecognized charts keep the Pair-based correlated_symbol.
    if _psp_auto_active
        correlated_symbol := psp_sym1_eff

    // A leg is live only if it is BOTH ticked and non-empty. The blank test is not cosmetic:
    // fetch_htf substitutes syminfo.tickerid for an empty symbol, so a blank leg returns the
    // chart's OWN data, which can never diverge from itself. Left ungated it would be counted as
    // a valid correlation that always agrees — harmless under ANY, but it would silence every PSP
    // and SMT under "Require all". Corr. 3 always had this test because it has always been able to
    // be blank; the leg switches above can now blank 2 as well, and a user can empty any of the
    // three by hand on an unrecognised chart.
    psp_sym1_enabled := psp_use1 and psp_sym1_eff != ""
    psp_sym2_enabled := psp_use2 and psp_sym2_eff != ""
    psp_sym3_enabled := psp_use3 and psp_sym3_eff != ""

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- PSP Correlated Data Requests (bull/bear direction per HTF per offset)                               ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
// 3 symbols × 6 HTFs = 18 security calls, plus the 6 chart-side calls the Strength Switch
// needs = 24. Each call returns direction (d0..d3) AND H/L for
// offsets 0..2 (h0/l0 .. h2/l2 — v4 added h2/l2 for the strength-switch failure-swing leg).
// Bundling here lets divergence + strength-switch detection reuse this data without burning
// more security calls. Offsets [0..3] match candles array indices (0 = current forming,
// 1 = last closed, etc.).
//
// extracted into fetch_htf() to remove ~7,000 chars of near-duplicate code.
// An empty symbol falls back to syminfo.tickerid so the call always has a valid one. That data is
// never used: an empty leg is excluded upstream by psp_symN_enabled, which requires a non-empty
// symbol as well as a ticked box. Any of the three can be empty — the auto-fill leg switches
// blank 2 and 3, and an unrecognised chart can have any of them cleared by hand.
fetch_htf(string sym, string tf) =>
    request.security(sym == "" ? syminfo.tickerid : sym, tf, [(close > open ? 1.0 : 0.0), ((close > open)[1] ? 1.0 : 0.0), ((close > open)[2] ? 1.0 : 0.0), ((close > open)[3] ? 1.0 : 0.0), high, low, high[1], low[1], high[2], low[2], high[3], low[3], high[4], low[4], high[5], low[5]], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off, ignore_invalid_symbol=true)

// ("Memory limits exceeded" on high chart TFs, e.g. 4h): request.security on a
// timeframe BELOW the chart's own pulls intrabar data and is hugely memory-heavy. Any HTF slot
// lower than the chart is invalid (ValidTimeframe rejects htf < chart) and its data is unused,
// so request the chart timeframe instead for those — trivial, already loaded, and discarded
// downstream. HTFs >= chart (the normal LTF-chart case) are unchanged, so this is behavior-
// identical for intended use.
_chart_secs = timeframe.in_seconds()
htf_1r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_1) >= _chart_secs ? htf_1 : timeframe.period
htf_2r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_2) >= _chart_secs ? htf_2 : timeframe.period
htf_3r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_3) >= _chart_secs ? htf_3 : timeframe.period
htf_4r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_4) >= _chart_secs ? htf_4 : timeframe.period
htf_5r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_5) >= _chart_secs ? htf_5 : timeframe.period
htf_6r = timeframe.in_seconds(htf_6) >= _chart_secs ? htf_6 : timeframe.period

[psp1_s1_d0, psp1_s1_d1, psp1_s1_d2, psp1_s1_d3, psp1_s1_h0, psp1_s1_l0, psp1_s1_h1, psp1_s1_l1, psp1_s1_h2, psp1_s1_l2, psp1_s1_h3, psp1_s1_l3, psp1_s1_h4, psp1_s1_l4, psp1_s1_h5, psp1_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_1r)
[psp1_s2_d0, psp1_s2_d1, psp1_s2_d2, psp1_s2_d3, psp1_s2_h0, psp1_s2_l0, psp1_s2_h1, psp1_s2_l1, psp1_s2_h2, psp1_s2_l2, psp1_s2_h3, psp1_s2_l3, psp1_s2_h4, psp1_s2_l4, psp1_s2_h5, psp1_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_1r)
[psp1_s3_d0, psp1_s3_d1, psp1_s3_d2, psp1_s3_d3, psp1_s3_h0, psp1_s3_l0, psp1_s3_h1, psp1_s3_l1, psp1_s3_h2, psp1_s3_l2, psp1_s3_h3, psp1_s3_l3, psp1_s3_h4, psp1_s3_l4, psp1_s3_h5, psp1_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_1r)
[psp2_s1_d0, psp2_s1_d1, psp2_s1_d2, psp2_s1_d3, psp2_s1_h0, psp2_s1_l0, psp2_s1_h1, psp2_s1_l1, psp2_s1_h2, psp2_s1_l2, psp2_s1_h3, psp2_s1_l3, psp2_s1_h4, psp2_s1_l4, psp2_s1_h5, psp2_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_2r)
[psp2_s2_d0, psp2_s2_d1, psp2_s2_d2, psp2_s2_d3, psp2_s2_h0, psp2_s2_l0, psp2_s2_h1, psp2_s2_l1, psp2_s2_h2, psp2_s2_l2, psp2_s2_h3, psp2_s2_l3, psp2_s2_h4, psp2_s2_l4, psp2_s2_h5, psp2_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_2r)
[psp2_s3_d0, psp2_s3_d1, psp2_s3_d2, psp2_s3_d3, psp2_s3_h0, psp2_s3_l0, psp2_s3_h1, psp2_s3_l1, psp2_s3_h2, psp2_s3_l2, psp2_s3_h3, psp2_s3_l3, psp2_s3_h4, psp2_s3_l4, psp2_s3_h5, psp2_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_2r)
[psp3_s1_d0, psp3_s1_d1, psp3_s1_d2, psp3_s1_d3, psp3_s1_h0, psp3_s1_l0, psp3_s1_h1, psp3_s1_l1, psp3_s1_h2, psp3_s1_l2, psp3_s1_h3, psp3_s1_l3, psp3_s1_h4, psp3_s1_l4, psp3_s1_h5, psp3_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_3r)
[psp3_s2_d0, psp3_s2_d1, psp3_s2_d2, psp3_s2_d3, psp3_s2_h0, psp3_s2_l0, psp3_s2_h1, psp3_s2_l1, psp3_s2_h2, psp3_s2_l2, psp3_s2_h3, psp3_s2_l3, psp3_s2_h4, psp3_s2_l4, psp3_s2_h5, psp3_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_3r)
[psp3_s3_d0, psp3_s3_d1, psp3_s3_d2, psp3_s3_d3, psp3_s3_h0, psp3_s3_l0, psp3_s3_h1, psp3_s3_l1, psp3_s3_h2, psp3_s3_l2, psp3_s3_h3, psp3_s3_l3, psp3_s3_h4, psp3_s3_l4, psp3_s3_h5, psp3_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_3r)
[psp4_s1_d0, psp4_s1_d1, psp4_s1_d2, psp4_s1_d3, psp4_s1_h0, psp4_s1_l0, psp4_s1_h1, psp4_s1_l1, psp4_s1_h2, psp4_s1_l2, psp4_s1_h3, psp4_s1_l3, psp4_s1_h4, psp4_s1_l4, psp4_s1_h5, psp4_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_4r)
[psp4_s2_d0, psp4_s2_d1, psp4_s2_d2, psp4_s2_d3, psp4_s2_h0, psp4_s2_l0, psp4_s2_h1, psp4_s2_l1, psp4_s2_h2, psp4_s2_l2, psp4_s2_h3, psp4_s2_l3, psp4_s2_h4, psp4_s2_l4, psp4_s2_h5, psp4_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_4r)
[psp4_s3_d0, psp4_s3_d1, psp4_s3_d2, psp4_s3_d3, psp4_s3_h0, psp4_s3_l0, psp4_s3_h1, psp4_s3_l1, psp4_s3_h2, psp4_s3_l2, psp4_s3_h3, psp4_s3_l3, psp4_s3_h4, psp4_s3_l4, psp4_s3_h5, psp4_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_4r)
[psp5_s1_d0, psp5_s1_d1, psp5_s1_d2, psp5_s1_d3, psp5_s1_h0, psp5_s1_l0, psp5_s1_h1, psp5_s1_l1, psp5_s1_h2, psp5_s1_l2, psp5_s1_h3, psp5_s1_l3, psp5_s1_h4, psp5_s1_l4, psp5_s1_h5, psp5_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_5r)
[psp5_s2_d0, psp5_s2_d1, psp5_s2_d2, psp5_s2_d3, psp5_s2_h0, psp5_s2_l0, psp5_s2_h1, psp5_s2_l1, psp5_s2_h2, psp5_s2_l2, psp5_s2_h3, psp5_s2_l3, psp5_s2_h4, psp5_s2_l4, psp5_s2_h5, psp5_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_5r)
[psp5_s3_d0, psp5_s3_d1, psp5_s3_d2, psp5_s3_d3, psp5_s3_h0, psp5_s3_l0, psp5_s3_h1, psp5_s3_l1, psp5_s3_h2, psp5_s3_l2, psp5_s3_h3, psp5_s3_l3, psp5_s3_h4, psp5_s3_l4, psp5_s3_h5, psp5_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_5r)
[psp6_s1_d0, psp6_s1_d1, psp6_s1_d2, psp6_s1_d3, psp6_s1_h0, psp6_s1_l0, psp6_s1_h1, psp6_s1_l1, psp6_s1_h2, psp6_s1_l2, psp6_s1_h3, psp6_s1_l3, psp6_s1_h4, psp6_s1_l4, psp6_s1_h5, psp6_s1_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym1_eff, htf_6r)
[psp6_s2_d0, psp6_s2_d1, psp6_s2_d2, psp6_s2_d3, psp6_s2_h0, psp6_s2_l0, psp6_s2_h1, psp6_s2_l1, psp6_s2_h2, psp6_s2_l2, psp6_s2_h3, psp6_s2_l3, psp6_s2_h4, psp6_s2_l4, psp6_s2_h5, psp6_s2_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym2_eff, htf_6r)
[psp6_s3_d0, psp6_s3_d1, psp6_s3_d2, psp6_s3_d3, psp6_s3_h0, psp6_s3_l0, psp6_s3_h1, psp6_s3_l1, psp6_s3_h2, psp6_s3_l2, psp6_s3_h3, psp6_s3_l3, psp6_s3_h4, psp6_s3_l4, psp6_s3_h5, psp6_s3_l5] = fetch_htf(psp_sym3_eff, htf_6r)

// The chart symbol's own HTF data (same shape) — the candles array only holds
// max_display candles, which is too few for the strength-switch sweep lookback. 6 more calls
// = 24 total, still well under the 40-call cap. (d2/d3 unused for the chart side.)
//
// Gated on show_ss. request.security cannot live inside an if, so the call always exists; what
// the toggle changes is what it COSTS. With SS off every one of these is redirected to the chart's
// own symbol at the chart's own timeframe — data TradingView has already loaded — so it resolves
// to near nothing. Exactly the htf_Nr swap, applied for the same reason: the six extra
// calls were the stated price of carrying this feature, and this is what stops an unticked
// toggle from paying it, and keeps the memory headroom that the request-consolidation work bought.
ss_tf1 = show_ss ? htf_1r : timeframe.period
ss_tf2 = show_ss ? htf_2r : timeframe.period
ss_tf3 = show_ss ? htf_3r : timeframe.period
ss_tf4 = show_ss ? htf_4r : timeframe.period
ss_tf5 = show_ss ? htf_5r : timeframe.period
ss_tf6 = show_ss ? htf_6r : timeframe.period
[cht1_d0, cht1_d1, cht1_d2, cht1_d3, cht1_h0, cht1_l0, cht1_h1, cht1_l1, cht1_h2, cht1_l2, cht1_h3, cht1_l3, cht1_h4, cht1_l4, cht1_h5, cht1_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf1)
[cht2_d0, cht2_d1, cht2_d2, cht2_d3, cht2_h0, cht2_l0, cht2_h1, cht2_l1, cht2_h2, cht2_l2, cht2_h3, cht2_l3, cht2_h4, cht2_l4, cht2_h5, cht2_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf2)
[cht3_d0, cht3_d1, cht3_d2, cht3_d3, cht3_h0, cht3_l0, cht3_h1, cht3_l1, cht3_h2, cht3_l2, cht3_h3, cht3_l3, cht3_h4, cht3_l4, cht3_h5, cht3_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf3)
[cht4_d0, cht4_d1, cht4_d2, cht4_d3, cht4_h0, cht4_l0, cht4_h1, cht4_l1, cht4_h2, cht4_l2, cht4_h3, cht4_l3, cht4_h4, cht4_l4, cht4_h5, cht4_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf4)
[cht5_d0, cht5_d1, cht5_d2, cht5_d3, cht5_h0, cht5_l0, cht5_h1, cht5_l1, cht5_h2, cht5_l2, cht5_h3, cht5_l3, cht5_h4, cht5_l4, cht5_h5, cht5_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf5)
[cht6_d0, cht6_d1, cht6_d2, cht6_d3, cht6_h0, cht6_l0, cht6_h1, cht6_l1, cht6_h2, cht6_l2, cht6_h3, cht6_l3, cht6_h4, cht6_l4, cht6_h5, cht6_l5] = fetch_htf("", ss_tf6)

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- HTF Rollover Detection (global scope)                                                                ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
// extracted from Monitor() so the ta.change / history-referencing time() calls
// run unconditionally on every bar (silences the "should be called on each calculation"
// compiler warnings at the six Monitor call sites). Logic carried over verbatim, including
// the custom-daily override that applies only to the '1D' HTF.
bool _cd_midnight = dayofweek(time, 'America/New_York') != dayofweek(time - (time - time[1]), 'America/New_York')
bool _cd_830      = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0830-0831:123456", 'America/New_York')) and na(time(timeframe.period, "0830-0831:123456", 'America/New_York')[1])
bool _cd_930      = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-0931:123456", 'America/New_York')) and na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-0931:123456", 'America/New_York')[1])
bool _custom_daily_new = settings.custom_daily == 'Midnight' ? _cd_midnight : settings.custom_daily == '8:30' ? _cd_830 : _cd_930

// Standard rollover = HTF bar-time change; the custom-daily override replaces it for '1D' when enabled.
newHTFCandle(string tf, bool rolled) =>
    settings.use_custom_daily and tf == '1D' ? _custom_daily_new : rolled

bool _new_htf1 = newHTFCandle(htf_1, ta.change(time(htf_1, 'America/New_York')) > 0)
bool _new_htf2 = newHTFCandle(htf_2, ta.change(time(htf_2, 'America/New_York')) > 0)
bool _new_htf3 = newHTFCandle(htf_3, ta.change(time(htf_3, 'America/New_York')) > 0)
bool _new_htf4 = newHTFCandle(htf_4, ta.change(time(htf_4, 'America/New_York')) > 0)
bool _new_htf5 = newHTFCandle(htf_5, ta.change(time(htf_5, 'America/New_York')) > 0)
bool _new_htf6 = newHTFCandle(htf_6, ta.change(time(htf_6, 'America/New_York')) > 0)

var Helper helper = Helper.new()  // was plain `Helper helper`; promoted to `var` so cache fields persist across bars
var Trace trace = Trace.new()
color color_transparent = #ffffff00

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Internal Functions                                                                                   ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

method LineStyle(Helper helper, string style) =>
    helper.name := style  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    out = switch style
        '----' => line.style_dashed
        '····' => line.style_dotted
        => line.style_solid
    out

shortSymbol(string sym) =>
    string s = sym
    s := str.replace_all(s, "CME_MINI:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "CBOT_MINI:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "COMEX:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "NYMEX:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "FX_IDC:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "FOREXCOM:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "NASDAQ:", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "BYBIT:", "")
    // Drop the metal base (XAU=gold, XAG=silver) so XAUUSD/XAGEUR display as just USD/EUR on metal charts.
    s := str.replace_all(s, "XAU", "")
    s := str.replace_all(s, "XAG", "")
    s

// Display names ("1!" stripped) reused by every PSP / divergence label.
// computed once — psp_symN_eff are fixed after bar 0, and ~33 str.replace_all calls
// per bar across a full history load is measurable waste against the execution-time budget.
var string psp_sym1_short = ""
var string psp_sym2_short = ""
var string psp_sym3_short = ""
if barstate.isfirst
    psp_sym1_short := str.replace_all(shortSymbol(psp_sym1_eff), "1!", "")
    psp_sym2_short := str.replace_all(shortSymbol(psp_sym2_eff), "1!", "")
    psp_sym3_short := str.replace_all(shortSymbol(psp_sym3_eff), "1!", "")

method DayofWeek(Helper helper, int index) =>
    helper.name := 'DOW'  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    switch
        index == 1 => 'M'
        index == 2 => 'T'
        index == 3 => 'W'
        index == 4 => 'T'
        index == 5 => 'F'
        index == 6 => 'S'
        index == 7 => 'S'
        na(index) => ''

method ValidTimeframe(Helper helper, string HTF) =>
    helper.name := HTF  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    if timeframe.in_seconds(HTF) >= timeframe.in_seconds('D') and timeframe.in_seconds(HTF) > timeframe.in_seconds()
        true
    else
        n1 = timeframe.in_seconds()
        n2 = timeframe.in_seconds(HTF)
        n1 < n2 and math.round(n2 / n1) == n2 / n1


method RemainingTime(Helper helper, string HTF) =>
    helper.name := HTF  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    if barstate.isrealtime
        timeRemaining = (time_close(HTF) - timenow) / 1000
        days = math.floor(timeRemaining / 86400)
        hours = math.floor((timeRemaining - days * 86400) / 3600)
        minutes = math.floor((timeRemaining - days * 86400 - hours * 3600) / 60)
        seconds = math.floor(timeRemaining - days * 86400 - hours * 3600 - minutes * 60)

        r = str.tostring(seconds, '00')
        if minutes > 0 or hours > 0 or days > 0
            r := str.tostring(minutes, '00') + ':' + r
            r
        if hours > 0 or days > 0
            r := str.tostring(hours, '00') + ':' + r
            r
        if days > 0
            r := str.tostring(days) + 'D ' + r
            r
        r
    else
        'n/a'

method HTFName(Helper helper, string HTF) =>
    helper.name := 'HTFName'  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    formatted = HTF

    seconds = timeframe.in_seconds(HTF)
    int mins = math.round(seconds / 60)
    if seconds < 60
        formatted := str.tostring(seconds) + 's'
        formatted
    else if mins < 60
        formatted := str.tostring(mins) + 'm'
        formatted
    else if mins < 1440
        // Whole hours read as 1H / 4H / 6H. Anything that would come out fractional stays in
        // MINUTES — 90m is called 90m, not "1.5H", which is how the timeframe is actually referred
        // to. Everything from a day up keeps the raw timeframe string ('1D', '1W', …).
        formatted := mins % 60 == 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(mins / 60)) + 'H' : str.tostring(mins) + 'm'
        formatted
    formatted

method HTFEnabled(Helper helper) =>
    helper.name := 'HTFEnabled'  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    int enabled = 0
    enabled := enabled + (htf1.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    enabled := enabled + (htf2.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    enabled := enabled + (htf3.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    enabled := enabled + (htf4.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    enabled := enabled + (htf5.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    enabled := enabled + (htf6.settings.show ? 1 : 0)
    int last = math.min(enabled, settings.max_sets)

    last

method CandleSetHigh(Helper helper, array<Candle> candles, float h) =>
    helper.name := 'CandlesSetHigh'  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    float _h = h
    if array.size(candles) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(candles) - 1 by 1
            Candle c = array.get(candles, i)
            if c.h > _h
                _h := c.h
    _h

method CandleSetLow(Helper helper, array<Candle> candles, float l) =>
    helper.name := 'CandlesSetLow'  // Pine v6 first-arg-usage requirement
    float _l = l
    if array.size(candles) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(candles) - 1 by 1
            Candle c = array.get(candles, i)
            if c.l < _l
                _l := c.l
    _l

method CandlesHigh(Helper helper, array<Candle> candles) =>
    h = 0.0
    int cnt = 0
    int last = helper.htf_enabled_count  // cached

    if helper.htf1_active
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf1.candles, h)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf2_active and cnt < last
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf2.candles, h)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf3_active and cnt < last
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf3.candles, h)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf4_active and cnt < last
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf4.candles, h)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf5_active and cnt < last
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf5.candles, h)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf6_active and cnt < last
        h := helper.CandleSetHigh(htf6.candles, h)

    if array.size(candles) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(candles) - 1 by 1
            Candle c = array.get(candles, i)
            if c.h > h
                h := c.h
    h

method CandlesLow(Helper helper, array<Candle> candles, float h) =>
    l = h
    int cnt = 0
    int last = helper.htf_enabled_count  // cached

    if helper.htf1_active
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf1.candles, l)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf2_active and cnt < last
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf2.candles, l)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf3_active and cnt < last
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf3.candles, l)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf4_active and cnt < last
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf4.candles, l)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf5_active and cnt < last
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf5.candles, l)
        cnt := cnt + 1
    if helper.htf6_active and cnt < last
        l := helper.CandleSetLow(htf6.candles, l)

    if array.size(candles) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(candles) - 1 by 1
            Candle c = array.get(candles, i)
            if c.l < l
                l := c.l
    l

method UpdateTime(CandleSet candleSet, int offset) =>
    // Always update timer on last bar for visibility after resume
    if settings.htf_timer_show and barstate.islast
        string tmr = '[' + helper.RemainingTime(candleSet.settings.htf) + ']'

        if not na(candleSet.tfTimerTop)
            candleSet.tfTimerTop.set_text(tmr)

        if not na(candleSet.tfTimerBottom)
            candleSet.tfTimerBottom.set_text(tmr)
    candleSet

method Reorder(CandleSet candleSet, int offset) =>
    size = candleSet.candles.size()

    if size > 0
        for i = size - 1 to 0 by 1
            Candle candle = candleSet.candles.get(i)
            t_buffer = offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - i - 1)
            box.set_left(candle.body, bar_index + t_buffer)
            box.set_right(candle.body, bar_index + settings.width + t_buffer)
            line.set_x1(candle.wick_up, bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer)
            line.set_x2(candle.wick_up, bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer)
            line.set_x1(candle.wick_down, bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer)
            line.set_x2(candle.wick_down, bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer)

            // Rebuild Y-geometry + colors from the tracked o/c/h/l for EVERY candle.
            // Before drawing was deferred to the last bar, closed candles kept correct geometry only because Update() refreshed the
            // forming candle on every historical bar before it closed. With drawing deferred to the
            // last bar, closed candles would otherwise be stuck with their creation-bar values (the
            // first chart bar of their HTF period), rendering tiny/garbled bodies and wicks.
            bool candle_bull = candle.c > candle.o
            box.set_top(candle.body, candle.o)
            box.set_bottom(candle.body, candle.c)
            box.set_bgcolor(candle.body, candle_bull ? settings.bull_body : settings.bear_body)
            box.set_border_color(candle.body, candle_bull ? settings.bull_border : settings.bear_border)
            line.set_color(candle.wick_up, candle_bull ? settings.bull_wick : settings.bear_wick)
            line.set_color(candle.wick_down, candle_bull ? settings.bull_wick : settings.bear_wick)
            line.set_y1(candle.wick_up, candle.h)
            line.set_y2(candle.wick_up, math.max(candle.o, candle.c))
            line.set_y1(candle.wick_down, candle.l)
            line.set_y2(candle.wick_down, math.min(candle.o, candle.c))

            if settings.daily_name // and candleSet.settings.htf == '1D'
                if not na(candle.dow_label)
                    candle.dow_label.set_y(candle.l)
                    candle.dow_label.set_x(bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer)
                    candle.dow_label.set_text(candle.dow)
                else
                    candle.dow_label := label.new(bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer, candle.l, candle.dow, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.dow_color, style = label.style_label_up, size = settings.dow_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
            
            // 3-candle pattern: c1 makes range, c2 swings, c3 (THIS candle) set to expand
            if i < size - 2
                Candle c2 = candleSet.candles.get(i + 1)  // Candle 2 (swing candle)
                Candle c1 = candleSet.candles.get(i + 2)  // Candle 1 (range maker)
                
                // Check if c2 has a swing relative to c1
                bool c2_swing_high = c2.h > c1.h and c2.c < c1.h  // Bearish swing on c2
                bool c2_swing_low = c2.l < c1.l and c2.c > c1.l   // Bullish swing on c2
                
                // Color THIS candle (c3) based on c2's swing (expansion expected)
                if color_candles_by_swing
                    if c2_swing_high and c2_swing_low
                        box.set_bgcolor(candle.body, both_swing_color)
                    else if c2_swing_low
                        box.set_bgcolor(candle.body, bullish_swing_color)  // Expect bullish expansion after swing low
                    else if c2_swing_high
                        box.set_bgcolor(candle.body, bearish_swing_color)  // Expect bearish expansion after swing high
                    else
                        // Reset to default color if no swing
                        bool bull = candle.c > candle.o
                        box.set_bgcolor(candle.body, bull ? settings.bull_body : settings.bear_body)
            
            // Check if NEXT candle creates a swing on THIS candle (for drawing swing lines)
            // Include all candles except index 0 (most recent)
            if show_swing_lines and i >= 1
                Candle next_candle = candleSet.candles.get(i - 1)
                
                // Potential swing: next candle (forming) swept high, regardless of close position
                bool is_potential_high = i == 1 and next_candle.h > candle.h
                // Confirmed swing: next candle is closed and swept with rejection
                bool is_confirmed_high = i > 1 and next_candle.h > candle.h and next_candle.c < candle.h
                
                bool is_potential_low = i == 1 and next_candle.l < candle.l
                bool is_confirmed_low = i > 1 and next_candle.l < candle.l and next_candle.c > candle.l
                
                // Swing high line (show both potential and confirmed)
                if is_potential_high or is_confirmed_high
                    int next_buffer = offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - (i - 1) - 1)
                    int line_start = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer
                    int line_end = bar_index + next_buffer + settings.width + swing_overshoot
                    string line_style = is_confirmed_high ? confirmed_swing_style_value : potential_swing_style_value
                    
                    if na(candle.swing_high_line)
                        candle.swing_high_line := line.new(line_start, candle.h, line_end, candle.h, color=swing_high_color, width=swing_line_width, style=line_style)
                    else
                        line.set_x1(candle.swing_high_line, line_start)
                        line.set_y1(candle.swing_high_line, candle.h)
                        line.set_x2(candle.swing_high_line, line_end)
                        line.set_y2(candle.swing_high_line, candle.h)
                        line.set_style(candle.swing_high_line, line_style)
                else
                    // Delete only if confirmed closed candle invalidated the swing
                    if i > 1 and not na(candle.swing_high_line)
                        line.delete(candle.swing_high_line)
                        candle.swing_high_line := na
                
                // Swing low line (show both potential and confirmed)
                if is_potential_low or is_confirmed_low
                    int next_buffer = offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - (i - 1) - 1)
                    int line_start = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + t_buffer
                    int line_end = bar_index + next_buffer + settings.width + swing_overshoot
                    string line_style = is_confirmed_low ? confirmed_swing_style_value : potential_swing_style_value
                    
                    if na(candle.swing_low_line)
                        candle.swing_low_line := line.new(line_start, candle.l, line_end, candle.l, color=swing_low_color, width=swing_line_width, style=line_style)
                    else
                        line.set_x1(candle.swing_low_line, line_start)
                        line.set_y1(candle.swing_low_line, candle.l)
                        line.set_x2(candle.swing_low_line, line_end)
                        line.set_y2(candle.swing_low_line, candle.l)
                        line.set_style(candle.swing_low_line, line_style)
                else
                    // Delete only if confirmed closed candle invalidated the swing
                    if i > 1 and not na(candle.swing_low_line)
                        line.delete(candle.swing_low_line)
                        candle.swing_low_line := na
            
            // Draw EQ line from each closed candle to the next candle
            if show_eq_line and i >= 1 and size >= 2
                // This candle's equilibrium (midpoint of high and low)
                float eq_price = (candle.h + candle.l) / 2

                // Line from right edge of this candle to left edge of next candle (toward index 0)
                int next_buffer = offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - (i - 1) - 1)
                int line_start_x = bar_index + settings.width + t_buffer
                int line_end_x = bar_index + next_buffer

                if na(candle.eq_line)
                    candle.eq_line := line.new(line_start_x, eq_price, line_end_x, eq_price, color=eq_line_color, width=eq_line_width, style=eq_line_style_value)
                else
                    line.set_x1(candle.eq_line, line_start_x)
                    line.set_y1(candle.eq_line, eq_price)
                    line.set_x2(candle.eq_line, line_end_x)
                    line.set_y2(candle.eq_line, eq_price)
            // Clean up orphan EQ lines when show_eq_line is toggled off mid-session
            // (or when the candle moved into the i==0 / size<2 region where no EQ should draw).
            // Previously the line stayed until the indicator was reloaded.
            else if not na(candle.eq_line)
                line.delete(candle.eq_line)
                candle.eq_line := na
            
            // Column SMTs now live in the global col_smts pool (rebuilt each
            // last-bar tick), so there is no per-candle divergence cleanup to do here.
    top = 0.0
    bottom = 0.0

    if settings.label_alignment == 'Align'
        top := helper.CandlesHigh(candleSet.candles)
        bottom := helper.CandlesLow(candleSet.candles, top)
    if settings.label_alignment == 'Follow Candles'
        top := helper.CandleSetHigh(candleSet.candles, 0)
        bottom := helper.CandleSetLow(candleSet.candles, top)

    left = bar_index + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1) / 2

    // Always update labels on last bar for visibility after resume
    if settings.htf_label_show and barstate.islast
        string lblt = helper.HTFName(candleSet.settings.htf)
        
        // Add swing icons if applicable
        if candleSet.candles.size() >= 2
            Candle last_candle = candleSet.candles.get(1)
            Candle current_candle = candleSet.candles.get(0)
            
            // Check for swing high
            bool high_broken = current_candle.h > last_candle.h
            bool close_rejected_high = current_candle.c < last_candle.h
            bool confirmed_swing_high = high_broken and close_rejected_high
            bool potential_swing_high = high_broken and not close_rejected_high
            
            // Check for swing low
            bool low_broken = current_candle.l < last_candle.l
            bool close_rejected_low = current_candle.c > last_candle.l
            bool confirmed_swing_low = low_broken and close_rejected_low
            bool potential_swing_low = low_broken and not close_rejected_low
            
            // Add appropriate icons
            if confirmed_swing_high
                lblt := lblt + " ▼"  // Filled triangle for confirmed
            else if potential_swing_high
                lblt := lblt + " ▽"  // Outlined triangle for potential
            
            if confirmed_swing_low
                lblt := lblt + " ▲"  // Filled triangle for confirmed
            else if potential_swing_low
                lblt := lblt + " △"  // Outlined triangle for potential
        
        string lbll = lblt
        if settings.htf_timer_show
            lblt := lblt + '\n'
            lbll := '\n' + lbll
        if settings.daily_name
            lblt := lblt + '\n'

        string tmr = '[' + helper.RemainingTime(candleSet.settings.htf) + ']' + (settings.daily_name ? '\n' : '')
        if settings.label_position == 'Both' or settings.label_position == 'Top'
            
            if not na(candleSet.tfNameTop)
                candleSet.tfNameTop.set_xy(left, top)
                candleSet.tfNameTop.set_text(lblt)  // Update text to include swing icons
            else
                if htf_label_bold
                    candleSet.tfNameTop := label.new(left, top, lblt, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_label_color, style = label.style_label_down, size = settings.htf_label_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace, text_formatting = text.format_bold)
                else
                    candleSet.tfNameTop := label.new(left, top, lblt, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_label_color, style = label.style_label_down, size = settings.htf_label_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
            if settings.htf_timer_show
                if not na(candleSet.tfTimerTop)
                    candleSet.tfTimerTop.set_xy(left, top)
                else
                    candleSet.tfTimerTop := label.new(left, top, tmr, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_timer_color, style = label.style_label_down, size = settings.htf_timer_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)

        if settings.label_position == 'Both' or settings.label_position == 'Bottom'
            if not na(candleSet.tfNameBottom)
                candleSet.tfNameBottom.set_xy(left, bottom)
                candleSet.tfNameBottom.set_text(lbll)  // Update text to include swing icons
            else
                if htf_label_bold
                    candleSet.tfNameBottom := label.new(left, bottom, lbll, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_label_color, style = label.style_label_up, size = settings.htf_label_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace, text_formatting = text.format_bold)
                else
                    candleSet.tfNameBottom := label.new(left, bottom, lbll, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_label_color, style = label.style_label_up, size = settings.htf_label_size, text_font_family = font.family_monospace)
            if settings.htf_timer_show
                if not na(candleSet.tfTimerBottom)
                    candleSet.tfTimerBottom.set_xy(left, bottom)
                else
                    candleSet.tfTimerBottom := label.new(left, bottom, tmr, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.htf_timer_color, style = label.style_label_up, size = settings.htf_timer_size)

    candleSet

method FindImbalance(CandleSet candleSet) =>
    // Always run on last bar to ensure visibility after resume
    if barstate.islast
        if candleSet.imbalances.size() > 0
            for i = candleSet.imbalances.size() - 1 to 0 by 1
                Imbalance del = candleSet.imbalances.get(i)
                box.delete(del.b)
                candleSet.imbalances.pop()

        if candleSet.candles.size() > 3 and settings.fvg_show
            for i = 0 to candleSet.candles.size() - 3 by 1
                candle1 = candleSet.candles.get(i)
                candle2 = candleSet.candles.get(i + 2)
                candle3 = candleSet.candles.get(i + 1)

                if candle1.l > candle2.h and math.min(candle1.o, candle1.c) > math.max(candle2.o, candle2.c)
                    Imbalance imb = Imbalance.new()
                    imb.b := box.new(box.get_left(candle2.body), candle2.h, box.get_right(candle1.body), candle1.l, bgcolor = settings.fvg_color, border_color = color_transparent, xloc = xloc.bar_index)
                    candleSet.imbalances.push(imb)
                if candle1.h < candle2.l and math.max(candle1.o, candle1.c) < math.min(candle2.o, candle2.c)
                    Imbalance imb = Imbalance.new()
                    imb.b := box.new(box.get_right(candle1.body), candle1.h, box.get_left(candle2.body), candle2.l, bgcolor = settings.fvg_color, border_color = color_transparent)
                    candleSet.imbalances.push(imb)
                box temp = box.copy(candle3.body)
                box.delete(candle3.body)
                candle3.body := temp

        if candleSet.candles.size() > 2 and settings.vi_show
            for i = 0 to candleSet.candles.size() - 2 by 1
                candle1 = candleSet.candles.get(i)
                candle2 = candleSet.candles.get(i + 1)
                if candle1.l < candle2.h and math.min(candle1.o, candle1.c) > math.max(candle2.o, candle2.c)
                    Imbalance imb = Imbalance.new()
                    imb.b := box.new(box.get_left(candle2.body), math.min(candle1.o, candle1.c), box.get_right(candle1.body), math.max(candle2.o, candle2.c), bgcolor = settings.vi_color, border_color = color_transparent)
                    candleSet.imbalances.push(imb)
                if candle1.h > candle2.l and math.max(candle1.o, candle1.c) < math.min(candle2.o, candle2.c)
                    Imbalance imb = Imbalance.new()
                    imb.b := box.new(box.get_right(candle1.body), math.min(candle2.o, candle2.c), box.get_left(candle2.body), math.max(candle1.o, candle1.c), bgcolor = settings.vi_color, border_color = color_transparent)
                    candleSet.imbalances.push(imb)
    candleSet

// Rollover detection moved to global scope (see "HTF Rollover Detection"
// section); Monitor now receives the pre-computed flag so it contains no series-stateful calls.
method Monitor(CandleSet candleSet, bool isNewHTFCandle) =>
    if isNewHTFCandle
        Candle candle = Candle.new()
        candle.o := open
        candle.c := close
        candle.h := high
        candle.l := low
        candle.o_time := time
        candle.o_idx := bar_index
        candle.c_idx := bar_index
        candle.h_idx := bar_index
        candle.l_idx := bar_index
        candle.has_bearish_div := false
        candle.has_bullish_div := false
        // Route on timeframe.in_seconds(), not str.tonumber(): '1W' / '7D' / '4H' / '3M' all
        // return na from str.tonumber(), which would make every numeric branch false and leave
        // those timeframes with a blank candle-time label.
        candle.dow := switch
            candleSet.settings.htf == '1D' =>
                helper.DayofWeek(dayofweek(time_tradingday, "America/New_York"))
            timeframe.in_seconds(candleSet.settings.htf) >= 86400 =>  // daily-or-greater (W, M, multi-day)
                str.format_time(candle.o_time, 'M/d', 'America/New_York')
            timeframe.in_seconds(candleSet.settings.htf) > 0 =>        // intraday (S / minutes / hours)
                str.format_time(candle.o_time, 'HH:mm', 'America/New_York')
            =>
                ''
        bull = candle.c > candle.o

        candle.body := box.new(bar_index, math.max(candle.o, candle.c), bar_index + 2, math.min(candle.o, candle.c), bull ? settings.bull_border : settings.bear_border, 1, bgcolor = bull ? settings.bull_body : settings.bear_body)
        candle.wick_up := line.new(bar_index + 1, candle.h, bar_index, math.max(candle.o, candle.c), color = bull ? settings.bull_wick : settings.bear_wick)
        candle.wick_down := line.new(bar_index + 1, math.min(candle.o, candle.c), bar_index, candle.l, color = bull ? settings.bull_wick : settings.bear_wick)

        candleSet.candles.unshift(candle)
        // Mirror into the 6-deep H/L history. Capped independently of max_display so the SMTF gap
        // test keeps its depth no matter how few candles the column draws.
        candleSet.hHist.unshift(candle.h)
        candleSet.lHist.unshift(candle.l)
        if candleSet.hHist.size() > 6
            candleSet.hHist.pop()
            candleSet.lHist.pop()

        if candleSet.candles.size() > candleSet.settings.max_display
            Candle delCandle = array.pop(candleSet.candles)
            box.delete(delCandle.body)
            line.delete(delCandle.wick_up)
            line.delete(delCandle.wick_down)
            if not na(delCandle.dow_label)
                label.delete(delCandle.dow_label)
            if not na(delCandle.swing_high_line)
                line.delete(delCandle.swing_high_line)
            if not na(delCandle.swing_low_line)
                line.delete(delCandle.swing_low_line)
            if not na(delCandle.eq_line)
                line.delete(delCandle.eq_line)
            if not na(delCandle.psp_label)
                label.delete(delCandle.psp_label)

    candleSet

method Update(CandleSet candleSet, int offset, bool showTrace) =>
    if candleSet.candles.size() > 0
        Candle candle = candleSet.candles.first()
        candle.h_idx := high > candle.h ? bar_index : candle.h_idx
        candle.h := high > candle.h ? high : candle.h
        candle.l_idx := low < candle.l ? bar_index : candle.l_idx
        candle.l := low < candle.l ? low : candle.l
        candle.c := close
        candle.c_idx := bar_index
        // Keep the forming candle's entry live so SMTF is tested against the DEVELOPING high/low
        // from the HTF candle's first tick, rather than waiting for a chart bar to close.
        if candleSet.hHist.size() > 0
            candleSet.hHist.set(0, candle.h)
            candleSet.lHist.set(0, candle.l)

        // All drawing work deferred to the last bar. Historical bars only track
        // candle data above; barstate.islast holds on every realtime tick AND on the final bar
        // of a fresh load, so visuals stay current and visibility-after-resume is preserved.
        // the per-candle body/wick geometry now lives in Reorder(), which rebuilds it
        // from the tracked o/c/h/l for ALL candles (not just the forming one).
        if barstate.islast
            candleSet.Reorder(offset)

            if settings.trace_show and showTrace
                if bar_index - candle.o_idx < 5000
                    if na(trace.o)
                        trace.o := line.new(candle.o_idx, candle.o, box.get_left(candle.body), candle.o, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = settings.trace_o_color, style = helper.LineStyle(settings.trace_o_style), width = settings.trace_o_size)
                        trace.o
                    else
                        line.set_xy1(trace.o, candle.o_idx, candle.o)
                        line.set_xy2(trace.o, box.get_left(candle.body), candle.o)

                    if settings.label_show
                        if na(trace.o_l)
                            trace.o_l := label.new(box.get_right(candle.body), candle.o, str.tostring(candle.o), textalign = text.align_center, style = label.style_label_left, size = settings.label_size, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.label_color)
                            trace.o_l
                        else
                            label.set_xy(trace.o_l, box.get_right(candle.body), candle.o)
                            label.set_text(trace.o_l, str.tostring(candle.o))

                if bar_index - candle.c_idx < 5000
                    if na(trace.c)
                        trace.c := line.new(candle.c_idx, candle.c, box.get_left(candle.body), candle.c, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = settings.trace_c_color, style = helper.LineStyle(settings.trace_c_style), width = settings.trace_c_size)
                        trace.c
                    else
                        line.set_xy1(trace.c, candle.c_idx, candle.c)
                        line.set_xy2(trace.c, box.get_left(candle.body), candle.c)

                    if settings.label_show
                        if na(trace.c_l)
                            trace.c_l := label.new(box.get_right(candle.body), candle.c, str.tostring(candle.c), textalign = text.align_center, style = label.style_label_left, size = settings.label_size, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.label_color)
                            trace.c_l
                        else
                            label.set_xy(trace.c_l, box.get_right(candle.body), candle.c)
                            label.set_text(trace.c_l, str.tostring(candle.c))

                if bar_index - candle.h_idx < 5000
                    if na(trace.h)
                        trace.h := line.new(candle.h_idx, candle.h, line.get_x1(candle.wick_up), candle.h, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = settings.trace_h_color, style = helper.LineStyle(settings.trace_h_style), width = settings.trace_h_size)
                        trace.h
                    else
                        line.set_xy1(trace.h, candle.h_idx, candle.h)
                        line.set_xy2(trace.h, line.get_x1(candle.wick_up), candle.h)

                    if settings.label_show
                        if na(trace.h_l)
                            trace.h_l := label.new(box.get_right(candle.body), candle.h, str.tostring(candle.h), textalign = text.align_center, style = label.style_label_left, size = settings.label_size, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.label_color)
                            trace.h_l
                        else
                            label.set_xy(trace.h_l, box.get_right(candle.body), candle.h)
                            label.set_text(trace.h_l, str.tostring(candle.h))

                if bar_index - candle.l_idx < 5000
                    if na(trace.l)
                        trace.l := line.new(candle.l_idx, candle.l, line.get_x1(candle.wick_down), candle.l, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = settings.trace_l_color, style = helper.LineStyle(settings.trace_l_style), width = settings.trace_l_size)
                        trace.l
                    else
                        line.set_xy1(trace.l, candle.l_idx, candle.l)
                        line.set_xy2(trace.l, line.get_x1(candle.wick_down), candle.l)

                    if settings.label_show
                        if na(trace.l_l)
                            trace.l_l := label.new(box.get_right(candle.body), candle.l, str.tostring(candle.l), textalign = text.align_center, style = label.style_label_left, size = settings.label_size, color = color_transparent, textcolor = settings.label_color)
                            trace.l_l
                        else
                            label.set_xy(trace.l_l, box.get_right(candle.body), candle.l)
                            label.set_text(trace.l_l, str.tostring(candle.l))
    candleSet

// Apply PSP (Precision Swing Point) detection and visuals to a CandleSet.
// Compares each candle's body direction (bull/bear) against up to three correlated symbols. Where
// they disagree the candle keeps its fill and takes a coloured BORDER, optionally haloed, plus a
// label naming the disagreeing correlations and this symbol's side (S strong / W weak).
// Evaluates index 0 (the currently forming HTF candle) too, so a PSP appears while it is still
// developing — in the Developing colour, since it can invalidate before the candle closes.
method ApplyPSP(CandleSet candleSet, float s1d0, float s1d1, float s1d2, float s1d3, float s2d0, float s2d1, float s2d2, float s2d3, float s3d0, float s3d1, float s3d2, float s3d3) =>
    n = candleSet.candles.size()
    // Evaluate forming candle (index 0) + recent closed candles (1..3).
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to math.min(n - 1, 3)
            Candle c = candleSet.candles.get(i)
            float c_bull = c.c > c.o ? 1.0 : 0.0

            float corr_s1 = switch i
                0 => s1d0
                1 => s1d1
                2 => s1d2
                => s1d3
            float corr_s2 = switch i
                0 => s2d0
                1 => s2d1
                2 => s2d2
                => s2d3
            float corr_s3 = switch i
                0 => s3d0
                1 => s3d1
                2 => s3d2
                => s3d3

            bool s1_valid = psp_sym1_enabled and not na(corr_s1)
            bool s2_valid = psp_sym2_enabled and not na(corr_s2)
            bool s3_valid = psp_sym3_enabled and not na(corr_s3)
            bool div1 = s1_valid and c_bull != corr_s1
            bool div2 = s2_valid and c_bull != corr_s2
            bool div3 = s3_valid and c_bull != corr_s3
            // "Require all" = every ENABLED correlation must diverge. An unticked or data-less
            // symbol is skipped rather than blocking the PSP, so unticking Corr. 1 and 2 leaves
            // a clean RTY-only test instead of killing PSP entirely.
            bool is_psp = psp_require_both
                 ? ((s1_valid or s2_valid or s3_valid) and (not s1_valid or div1) and (not s2_valid or div2) and (not s3_valid or div3))
                 : (div1 or div2 or div3)
            // Join multi-symbol PSP names with ' & ' to match the divergence
            // label format (e.g. "ES & YM W" instead of "ES+YM W").
            string psp_with = ""
            if div1
                psp_with := psp_sym1_short
            if div2
                psp_with := psp_with == "" ? psp_sym2_short : psp_with + " & " + psp_sym2_short
            if div3
                psp_with := psp_with == "" ? psp_sym3_short : psp_with + " & " + psp_sym3_short

            c.is_psp := is_psp

            if is_psp
                // Border only: the body keeps its inherited bull/bear/expansion fill. Filling the
                // background as well made PSP candles read as solid blocks, which buried the
                // information rather than highlighting it.
                // The forming candle (i == 0) is a DEVELOPING PSP and takes its own border colour.
                color psp_col = i == 0 ? psp_dev_border_color : psp_border_color
                // DetectStrengthSwitch may override this with the SS colour afterwards.
                box.set_border_color(c.body, psp_col)
                // Halo, following the candle SHAPE: a ring around the body, and a wider faded line
                // behind each wick. A single box from c.h to c.l would fence off the whole range
                // instead. Widest / faintest ring first so the tighter ones land on top; ring N is
                // N PIXELS wide — Pine centres box borders on the edge, so a wide ring bleeds well
                // past a 2-bar-wide candle and stops reading as a glow. The descending loop is
                // deliberate (Pine counts down when from > to).
                if psp_glow_show
                    int gl = box.get_left(c.body)
                    int gr = box.get_right(c.body)
                    int gx = line.get_x1(c.wick_up)
                    float gTop = math.max(c.o, c.c)
                    float gBot = math.min(c.o, c.c)
                    int gstep = math.round((95 - psp_glow_fade) / math.max(psp_glow_layers, 1))
                    for gi = psp_glow_layers to 1
                        int gt = math.min(95, psp_glow_fade + (gi - 1) * gstep)
                        color gc = color.new(psp_col, gt)
                        array.push(psp_glows, box.new(gl, gTop, gr, gBot, border_color=gc, border_width=gi, bgcolor=color_transparent, xloc=xloc.bar_index))
                        // Wick backing — one step wider than the ring so the 1px wick still reads
                        // against it. Skipped on a side with no wick (h == body top / l == body bottom).
                        if c.h > gTop
                            array.push(psp_glow_wicks, line.new(gx, c.h, gx, gTop, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=gc, width=gi + 1))
                        if c.l < gBot
                            array.push(psp_glow_wicks, line.new(gx, gBot, gx, c.l, xloc=xloc.bar_index, color=gc, width=gi + 1))
                    // Lift the wicks above their backing. Pine stacks drawings in creation order and
                    // the glow lines were just created, so without this the backing paints over the
                    // wick. Same copy-and-swap FindImbalance uses to raise bodies over imbalances.
                    line wuC = line.copy(c.wick_up)
                    line.delete(c.wick_up)
                    c.wick_up := wuC
                    line wdC = line.copy(c.wick_down)
                    line.delete(c.wick_down)
                    c.wick_down := wdC
                if psp_label_show
                    int lx    = box.get_left(c.body) + settings.width / 2
                    float ly  = c_bull == 1.0 ? c.h : c.l
                    string strength = c_bull == 1.0 ? "W" : "S"
                    string lt = psp_with + " " + strength
                    string ls = c_bull == 1.0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up
                    if na(c.psp_label)
                        c.psp_label := label.new(lx, ly, lt, color=color.new(color.white, 100), textcolor=psp_label_color, style=ls, size=psp_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                    else
                        c.psp_label.set_xy(lx, ly)
                        c.psp_label.set_text(lt)
                        c.psp_label.set_style(ls)
                    // An icon label used to stack above bullish / below bearish PSP candles.
                    // It was dropped: the text label already says everything it did.
            else
                c.is_psp := false
                if not na(c.psp_label)
                    label.delete(c.psp_label)
                    c.psp_label := na
                // Restore default/expansion body color — mirrors the Reorder() coloring branch.
                bool bull = c.c > c.o
                if i < n - 2 and color_candles_by_swing
                    Candle c2c = candleSet.candles.get(i + 1)
                    Candle c1c = candleSet.candles.get(i + 2)
                    bool c2_sh = c2c.h > c1c.h and c2c.c < c1c.h
                    bool c2_sl = c2c.l < c1c.l and c2c.c > c1c.l
                    if c2_sh and c2_sl
                        box.set_bgcolor(c.body, both_swing_color)
                    else if c2_sl
                        box.set_bgcolor(c.body, bullish_swing_color)
                    else if c2_sh
                        box.set_bgcolor(c.body, bearish_swing_color)
                    else
                        box.set_bgcolor(c.body, bull ? settings.bull_body : settings.bear_body)
                    box.set_border_color(c.body, bull ? settings.bull_border : settings.bear_border)
                else
                    box.set_bgcolor(c.body, bull ? settings.bull_body : settings.bear_body)
                    box.set_border_color(c.body, bull ? settings.bull_border : settings.bear_border)
    candleSet

// Highest / lowest of the first `n` values, na-tolerant — deeper history may be missing on
// early bars, in which case the valid shallower values still form the reference.
hiOf(int n, float a, float b, float c, float d) =>
    float m = a
    if n >= 2 and not na(b)
        m := na(m) ? b : math.max(m, b)
    if n >= 3 and not na(c)
        m := na(m) ? c : math.max(m, c)
    if n >= 4 and not na(d)
        m := na(m) ? d : math.max(m, d)
    m

loOf(int n, float a, float b, float c, float d) =>
    float m = a
    if n >= 2 and not na(b)
        m := na(m) ? b : math.min(m, b)
    if n >= 3 and not na(c)
        m := na(m) ? c : math.min(m, c)
    if n >= 4 and not na(d)
        m := na(m) ? d : math.min(m, d)
    m

// na-tolerant extreme of array values over the inclusive index range [frm, upto] (no-op when
// frm > upto). NB: `from`/`to` are reserved Pine keywords, so the params are frm/upto.
arrLo(array<float> a, int frm, int upto) =>
    float m = na
    if frm <= upto
        for k = frm to upto
            float v = a.get(k)
            if not na(v)
                m := na(m) ? v : math.min(m, v)
    m

arrHi(array<float> a, int frm, int upto) =>
    float m = na
    if frm <= upto
        for k = frm to upto
            float v = a.get(k)
            if not na(v)
                m := na(m) ? v : math.max(m, v)
    m

// Running prefix extremes: out.get(m) is the na-tolerant extreme of a[0..m], i.e. exactly what
// arrHi / arrLo(a, 0, m) return — but computed once for every m in a single pass instead of
// rescanning from 0 on each lookup.
//
// The `size > 0` guard is not decoration: `for k = 0 to -1` runs BACKWARDS in Pine, which is the
// same trap that produced the RE10045 out-of-bounds this file documents elsewhere.
preHi(array<float> a) =>
    array<float> o = array.new<float>(a.size(), na)
    float m = na
    if a.size() > 0
        for k = 0 to a.size() - 1
            float v = a.get(k)
            if not na(v)
                m := na(m) ? v : math.max(m, v)
            o.set(k, m)
    o

preLo(array<float> a) =>
    array<float> o = array.new<float>(a.size(), na)
    float m = na
    if a.size() > 0
        for k = 0 to a.size() - 1
            float v = a.get(k)
            if not na(v)
                m := na(m) ? v : math.min(m, v)
            o.set(k, m)
    o

// SMTF support — is `px` sitting inside a 3-candle fair value gap that formed BEFORE candle `t`?
// Index 0 is the newest candle, so a gap whose newest member sits at index a > t is older than the
// tip. The triple is (a, a+1, a+2) with a the newest; an up gap runs from the old candle's high to
// the new candle's low, a down gap the reverse. A gap the tip itself helps form (a == t) is
// deliberately excluded — the point of SMTF is delivery INTO an existing imbalance.
//
// ONE helper for every asset. It used to be two — the chart symbol was tested against its
// DISPLAYED column candles, so a 3-candle column (the default on HTF 3-6) could not test the
// chart side at all and a 4-candle one only reached the forming candle. That is why a 1H column
// never flagged SMTF off YM's own gaps while the 4-candle 30m did. The chart symbol now keeps its
// own 6-deep hHist/lHist, so both sides get the same depth and the test no longer depends on how
// many candles a column happens to show.
//
// The deepest valid `a` is size - 3, since a + 2 must stay in range. Deriving it from the array
// rather than hard-coding 3 is what makes a short, still-filling history safe (it simply yields a
// negative bound and the loop is skipped) — and it is the same off-by-one that produced RE10045.
symInGap(array<float> sh, array<float> sl, int t, float px) =>
    bool hit = false
    int last = math.min(sh.size(), sl.size()) - 3
    if t + 1 <= last
        for a = t + 1 to last
            float nh = sh.get(a)
            float nl = sl.get(a)
            float oh = sh.get(a + 2)
            float ol = sl.get(a + 2)
            if not na(nh) and not na(nl) and not na(oh) and not na(ol)
                if nl > oh and px >= oh and px <= nl
                    hit := true
                if nh < ol and px >= nh and px <= ol
                    hit := true
    hit

// SEQUENTIAL timeframes. Every cycle divides into four quarters, and each quarter is one candle of
// the timeframe below:
//  monthly cycle -> weekly candles weekly cycle  -> daily candles
//  daily cycle   -> 6H candles (the four sessions: Asia, London, NY AM, NY PM)
//  session cycle -> 90m candles 90m cycle     -> 22.5m candles
// A divergence between two CONSECUTIVE quarters of a cycle is a sequential SMT (SSMT) — the
// time-filtered version of SMT, and the one worth acting on. Anything else is a regular SMT.
//
// Gated by show_ssmt at BOTH call sites rather than here, so one flag off turns the whole feature
// off in one place: with isSeq false the prefix reverts to SMTF/plain, the tip-cap and label-filter
// exemptions fall away, and ChartSMTCand.isSsmt is never set, so the overlay merge ranks on
// timeframe alone again.
isSeqTF(int tfSecs) =>
    tfSecs == 1350 or tfSecs == 5400 or tfSecs == 21600 or tfSecs == 86400 or tfSecs == 604800

// SSMT is a CONSECUTIVE-quarter divergence, so `seq` must carry the adjacency test as well as the
// timeframe — an SMT that skips a quarter is a regular SMT no matter which timeframe it is on.

smtPrefix(bool seq, bool gap) =>
    seq ? (gap ? "SSMTF " : "SSMT ") : (gap ? "SMTF " : "")

// Detect SMT divergence on the HTF column — ALL-PAIRS model (, replacing the
// earlier nearest-anchor scheme). On the last bar, every pair of
// displayed candles (i = newer, j = older) within `div_lookback` of each other is tested
// independently, and each diverging pair draws its own line (+ symbol-name label) into the
// global col_smts pool. A single candle can therefore anchor several SMTs at once — e.g.
// C0-C1, C0-C2 AND C1-C2 all draw. The pool is cleared and rebuilt every last-bar tick
// (stateless — no rollover/persistence bookkeeping). Correlated-symbol data depth caps the
// window at offset 5 (6 candles); lines are further capped by the displayed candle count, so
// raise an HTF's candle-display count to see deeper pairs.
method DetectDivergence(CandleSet candleSet, int offset,
                        float s1_h0, float s1_l0, float s1_h1, float s1_l1, float s1_h2, float s1_l2, float s1_h3, float s1_l3, float s1_h4, float s1_l4, float s1_h5, float s1_l5,
                        float s2_h0, float s2_l0, float s2_h1, float s2_l1, float s2_h2, float s2_l2, float s2_h3, float s2_l3, float s2_h4, float s2_l4, float s2_h5, float s2_l5,
                        float s3_h0, float s3_l0, float s3_h1, float s3_l1, float s3_h2, float s3_l2, float s3_h3, float s3_l3, float s3_h4, float s3_l4, float s3_h5, float s3_l5) =>
    size = candleSet.candles.size()
    // Clear last tick's stashed SMT label/anchor on every candle BEFORE the
    // show_divergence gate. The col_smts pool is cleared unconditionally each last-bar tick, so
    // these handles must never outlive it (an earlier candleSet.smtLowLbl reset was ungated too).
    if barstate.islast and size > 0
        for r0 = 0 to size - 1
            Candle cr0 = candleSet.candles.get(r0)
            cr0.smt_low_lbl := na
            cr0.smt_high_lbl := na
            cr0.smt_low_anchor := -1
            cr0.smt_high_anchor := -1
    if show_divergence and size >= 2 and barstate.islast
        // Tuple params → indexable arrays (index = candle offset, 0 = forming).
        array<float> s1h = array.from(s1_h0, s1_h1, s1_h2, s1_h3, s1_h4, s1_h5)
        array<float> s1l = array.from(s1_l0, s1_l1, s1_l2, s1_l3, s1_l4, s1_l5)
        array<float> s2h = array.from(s2_h0, s2_h1, s2_h2, s2_h3, s2_h4, s2_h5)
        array<float> s2l = array.from(s2_l0, s2_l1, s2_l2, s2_l3, s2_l4, s2_l5)
        array<float> s3h = array.from(s3_h0, s3_h1, s3_h2, s3_h3, s3_h4, s3_h5)
        array<float> s3l = array.from(s3_l0, s3_l1, s3_l2, s3_l3, s3_l4, s3_l5)
        bool isSeq = show_ssmt and isSeqTF(timeframe.in_seconds(candleSet.settings.htf))

        // The level-break windows are prefix ranges [0, j-1]: they depend on the OLDER anchor j and
        // never on the tip i, so computing them inside the j loop redid the same seven scans for
        // every (i, j) pair. Hoisted to eight running-extreme arrays built once per call and then
        // read by index — identical values, an order of magnitude fewer scans per realtime tick.
        array<float> chH = array.new<float>(size, na)
        array<float> chL = array.new<float>(size, na)
        for q = 0 to size - 1
            Candle cq = candleSet.candles.get(q)
            chH.set(q, cq.h)
            chL.set(q, cq.l)
        array<float> chHiPre = preHi(chH)
        array<float> chLoPre = preLo(chL)
        array<float> s1hPre = preHi(s1h)
        array<float> s1lPre = preLo(s1l)
        array<float> s2hPre = preHi(s2h)
        array<float> s2lPre = preLo(s2l)
        array<float> s3hPre = preHi(s3h)
        array<float> s3lPre = preLo(s3l)

        // Reset per-candle divergence flags (the info-table reads the forming candle's).
        for r = 0 to size - 1
            Candle cr = candleSet.candles.get(r)
            cr.has_bearish_div := false
            cr.has_bullish_div := false

        // Cap the newer-candle index at 4, not 5. The correlated-symbol arrays hold
        // only 6 offsets (0..5) and a pair needs j > i, so the deepest valid newer candle is i=4
        // (pairing with j=5). Allowing i=5 made the inner `for j = i+1 to jMax` become `for j = 6 to
        // 5`, which Pine runs BACKWARDS (start > end), hitting s1h.get(6) → RE10045 out-of-bounds.
        // Capping at 4 loses no pairs (deepest is still C0..C5) and keeps the inner loop forward-only.
        // The loop covers every tip the data allows; div_max_tips gates DRAWING further down, and
        // an SSMT is exempt from it — sequential divergences are the ones worth acting on, so a
        // display filter must not be able to hide one.
        int iMax = math.min(size - 2, 4)
        for i = 0 to iMax
            Candle ci = candleSet.candles.get(i)
            float s1hi = s1h.get(i)
            float s1li = s1l.get(i)
            float s2hi = s2h.get(i)
            float s2li = s2l.get(i)
            float s3hi = s3h.get(i)
            float s3li = s3l.get(i)
            // Merge accumulators are PER TIP CANDLE — declared inside the i loop so
            // each diverging candle keeps its own merged SMT. In an earlier version they lived outside the loop
            // and the newest diverging i claimed the column's only line, so a confirmed SMT
            // between two CLOSED candles was silently discarded the moment a newer candle also
            // diverged (and could never be SS-tagged). j still ascends, so the last accepted j
            // remains the furthest anchor for this tip.
            // Within the tip cap? An SSMT overrides this (see iMax comment).
            bool tipOk = i < div_max_tips
            int mLoJ = -1
            int mHiJ = -1
            // Did THIS tip diverge with its immediately preceding candle? Recorded separately from
            // mLoJ/mHiJ because the merge keeps the FURTHEST anchor — without this, widening the
            // drawn span past the adjacent candle would silently drop the SSMT flag, the same way
            // the overlay merge used to hide SMTF behind a higher timeframe.
            bool mLoAdj = false
            bool mHiAdj = false
            bool mLb1 = false
            bool mLb2 = false
            bool mLb3 = false
            bool mHb1 = false
            bool mHb2 = false
            bool mHb3 = false
            int jMax = math.min(math.min(i + div_lookback, size - 1), 5)
            for j = i + 1 to jMax
                Candle cj = candleSet.candles.get(j)

                // Level-break invalidation. An SMT between i (newer) and
                // j (older) is only valid if NO OTHER candle in the window broke the compared
                // extreme — the segment's peak (high SMT) / trough (low SMT) must be the extreme of
                // the whole range from the forming candle (index 0) through the older anchor j.
                // The first version covered candles BETWEEN i and j; this widens the scan to [0, j-1] so a candle
                // NEWER than the tip that prints a higher-high / lower-low (i.e. a new high/low made
                // AFTER the SMT) also voids it — once the level is taken the divergence is dead.
                // Checked per asset (chart + each correlated symbol), reference = max/min of the two
                // endpoints. The tip i is included in the scan but is harmless (never breaks its own
                // reference). j (the anchor) is the loop's upper bound and excluded.
                float chHiMax = chHiPre.get(j - 1)
                float chLoMin = chLoPre.get(j - 1)
                bool chHiOk = na(chHiMax) or chHiMax <= math.max(ci.h, cj.h)
                bool chLoOk = na(chLoMin) or chLoMin >= math.min(ci.l, cj.l)
                float s1HiInt = s1hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s1LoInt = s1lPre.get(j - 1)
                float s2HiInt = s2hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s2LoInt = s2lPre.get(j - 1)
                float s3HiInt = s3hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s3LoInt = s3lPre.get(j - 1)

                // >= / <= rather than strict: an equal extreme on one side still registers
                // against a strict break on the other. ci = newer, cj = older.
                // chHiOk/chLoOk + sNHiOk/sNLoOk = the intermediate guard (per asset, per side).
                bool v1 = psp_sym1_enabled and not na(s1hi) and not na(s1li) and not na(s1h.get(j)) and not na(s1l.get(j))
                bool s1HiOk = na(s1HiInt) or s1HiInt <= math.max(s1hi, s1h.get(j))
                bool s1LoOk = na(s1LoInt) or s1LoInt >= math.min(s1li, s1l.get(j))
                bool bull1 = v1 and chLoOk and s1LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s1li < s1l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s1li > s1l.get(j)))
                bool bear1 = v1 and chHiOk and s1HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s1hi < s1h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s1hi > s1h.get(j)))
                bool v2 = psp_sym2_enabled and not na(s2hi) and not na(s2li) and not na(s2h.get(j)) and not na(s2l.get(j))
                bool s2HiOk = na(s2HiInt) or s2HiInt <= math.max(s2hi, s2h.get(j))
                bool s2LoOk = na(s2LoInt) or s2LoInt >= math.min(s2li, s2l.get(j))
                bool bull2 = v2 and chLoOk and s2LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s2li < s2l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s2li > s2l.get(j)))
                bool bear2 = v2 and chHiOk and s2HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s2hi < s2h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s2hi > s2h.get(j)))
                bool v3 = psp_sym3_enabled and not na(s3hi) and not na(s3li) and not na(s3h.get(j)) and not na(s3l.get(j))
                bool s3HiOk = na(s3HiInt) or s3HiInt <= math.max(s3hi, s3h.get(j))
                bool s3LoOk = na(s3LoInt) or s3LoInt >= math.min(s3li, s3l.get(j))
                bool bull3 = v3 and chLoOk and s3LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s3li < s3l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s3li > s3l.get(j)))
                bool bear3 = v3 and chHiOk and s3HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s3hi < s3h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s3hi > s3h.get(j)))
                // ANY vs ALL. With require-all, a symbol that is unticked or has no data (vN false)
                // is skipped, not counted as a failure — otherwise a blank Corr. 3 would silence
                // every SMT on the chart. At least one enabled symbol must still be present.
                bool bullHit = div_require_all ? ((v1 or v2 or v3) and (not v1 or bull1) and (not v2 or bull2) and (not v3 or bull3)) : (bull1 or bull2 or bull3)
                bool bearHit = div_require_all ? ((v1 or v2 or v3) and (not v1 or bear1) and (not v2 or bear2) and (not v3 or bear3)) : (bear1 or bear2 or bear3)

                if div_merge
                    // Record THIS tip's furthest diverging anchor per side.
                    // Ascending j keeps the widest span; one merged SMT per tip candle.
                    if bullHit
                        mLoJ := j
                        mLb1 := bull1
                        mLb2 := bull2
                        mLb3 := bull3
                        if j == i + 1
                            mLoAdj := true
                    if bearHit
                        mHiJ := j
                        mHb1 := bear1
                        mHb2 := bear2
                        mHb3 := bear3
                        if j == i + 1
                            mHiAdj := true
                else
                    string bull_text = ""
                    if bull1
                        bull_text := psp_sym1_short
                    if bull2
                        bull_text := bull_text == "" ? psp_sym2_short : bull_text + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                    if bull3
                        bull_text := bull_text == "" ? psp_sym3_short : bull_text + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                    string bear_text = ""
                    if bear1
                        bear_text := psp_sym1_short
                    if bear2
                        bear_text := bear_text == "" ? psp_sym2_short : bear_text + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                    if bear3
                        bear_text := bear_text == "" ? psp_sym3_short : bear_text + " & " + psp_sym3_short

                    // Endpoint x-centers within the HTF column (newer = i on the right, older = j).
                    int xiC = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - i)
                    int xjC = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - j)

                    if bullHit and (tipOk or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                        bool sfLo = false
                        if show_smtf
                            sfLo := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.l)
                            if not sfLo and bull1
                                sfLo := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1l.get(i))
                            if not sfLo and bull2
                                sfLo := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2l.get(i))
                            if not sfLo and bull3
                                sfLo := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3l.get(i))
                        bull_text := smtPrefix(isSeq and j == i + 1, sfLo) + bull_text
                        ColumnSMT cs = ColumnSMT.new()
                        cs.ln := line.new(xjC, cj.l, xiC, ci.l, color=div_low_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                        if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or sfLo or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                            cs.lbl := label.new(math.round((xiC + xjC) / 2.0), (ci.l + cj.l) / 2, bull_text, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                        array.push(col_smts, cs)
                        ci.has_bullish_div := true

                    if bearHit and (tipOk or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                        bool sfHi = false
                        if show_smtf
                            sfHi := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.h)
                            if not sfHi and bear1
                                sfHi := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1h.get(i))
                            if not sfHi and bear2
                                sfHi := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2h.get(i))
                            if not sfHi and bear3
                                sfHi := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3h.get(i))
                        bear_text := smtPrefix(isSeq and j == i + 1, sfHi) + bear_text
                        ColumnSMT cs = ColumnSMT.new()
                        cs.ln := line.new(xjC, cj.h, xiC, ci.h, color=div_high_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                        if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or sfHi or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                            cs.lbl := label.new(math.round((xiC + xjC) / 2.0), (ci.h + cj.h) / 2, bear_text, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                        array.push(col_smts, cs)
                        ci.has_bearish_div := true

            // Draw THIS tip's merged low / high SMT (merge mode only). Every
            // diverging candle keeps its own line, so a confirmed divergence between two closed
            // candles stays drawn instead of being discarded when a newer candle also diverges.
            if div_merge and mLoJ != -1 and (tipOk or (isSeq and mLoAdj))
                Candle cjL = candleSet.candles.get(mLoJ)
                string tL = ""
                if mLb1
                    tL := psp_sym1_short
                if mLb2
                    tL := tL == "" ? psp_sym2_short : tL + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                if mLb3
                    tL := tL == "" ? psp_sym3_short : tL + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                // SMTF — the divergence delivered into a pre-existing gap on the chart symbol or
                // on any symbol that actually diverged here. One side is enough.
                bool gapL = false
                if show_smtf
                    gapL := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.l)
                    if not gapL and mLb1
                        gapL := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1l.get(i))
                    if not gapL and mLb2
                        gapL := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2l.get(i))
                    if not gapL and mLb3
                        gapL := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3l.get(i))
                tL := smtPrefix(isSeq and mLoAdj, gapL) + tL
                int xLi = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - i)
                int xLj = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - mLoJ)
                ColumnSMT csL = ColumnSMT.new()
                csL.ln := line.new(xLj, cjL.l, xLi, ci.l, color=div_low_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or gapL or (isSeq and mLoAdj))
                    csL.lbl := label.new(math.round((xLi + xLj) / 2.0), (ci.l + cjL.l) / 2, tL, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                array.push(col_smts, csL)
                ci.has_bullish_div := true
                ci.smt_low_lbl := csL.lbl
                ci.smt_low_anchor := mLoJ
            if div_merge and mHiJ != -1 and (tipOk or (isSeq and mHiAdj))
                Candle cjH = candleSet.candles.get(mHiJ)
                string tH = ""
                if mHb1
                    tH := psp_sym1_short
                if mHb2
                    tH := tH == "" ? psp_sym2_short : tH + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                if mHb3
                    tH := tH == "" ? psp_sym3_short : tH + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                // SMTF on the high side — same test against the candle's high.
                bool gapH = false
                if show_smtf
                    gapH := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.h)
                    if not gapH and mHb1
                        gapH := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1h.get(i))
                    if not gapH and mHb2
                        gapH := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2h.get(i))
                    if not gapH and mHb3
                        gapH := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3h.get(i))
                tH := smtPrefix(isSeq and mHiAdj, gapH) + tH
                int xHi = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - i)
                int xHj = bar_index + settings.width / 2 + offset + (settings.width + settings.buffer) * (size - 1 - mHiJ)
                ColumnSMT csH = ColumnSMT.new()
                csH.ln := line.new(xHj, cjH.h, xHi, ci.h, color=div_high_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or gapH or (isSeq and mHiAdj))
                    csH.lbl := label.new(math.round((xHi + xHj) / 2.0), (ci.h + cjH.h) / 2, tH, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                array.push(col_smts, csH)
                ci.has_bearish_div := true
                ci.smt_high_lbl := csH.lbl
                ci.smt_high_anchor := mHiJ
    candleSet

// Per-HTF chart-overlay divergence. now runs the SAME pair scan as the column
// detector (DetectDivergence) — div_lookback window, per-asset level-break invalidation, and
// merge (tip -> furthest valid anchor when div_merge is ON) — but anchors each line on the chart
// candles' real high/low bar indices (h_idx / l_idx) instead of the synthetic HTF column x, so the
// line spans the actual multi-candle swing the divergence sits on. It ONLY draws — it does not set
// has_*_div (those belong to DetectDivergence for the info table + SS-PSP two-stage read), so the
// strength-switch logic is unaffected. Each drawn SMT is one ChartDivergence row in chart_divs.
method DetectChartDivergence(CandleSet candleSet,
                              float s1_h0, float s1_l0, float s1_h1, float s1_l1, float s1_h2, float s1_l2, float s1_h3, float s1_l3, float s1_h4, float s1_l4, float s1_h5, float s1_l5,
                              float s2_h0, float s2_l0, float s2_h1, float s2_l1, float s2_h2, float s2_l2, float s2_h3, float s2_l3, float s2_h4, float s2_l4, float s2_h5, float s2_l5,
                              float s3_h0, float s3_l0, float s3_h1, float s3_l1, float s3_h2, float s3_l2, float s3_h3, float s3_l3, float s3_h4, float s3_l4, float s3_h5, float s3_l5) =>
    size = candleSet.candles.size()
    if size >= 2
        string tfName = helper.HTFName(candleSet.settings.htf)
        int tfSecs = timeframe.in_seconds(candleSet.settings.htf)  // merge precedence
        array<float> s1h = array.from(s1_h0, s1_h1, s1_h2, s1_h3, s1_h4, s1_h5)
        array<float> s1l = array.from(s1_l0, s1_l1, s1_l2, s1_l3, s1_l4, s1_l5)
        array<float> s2h = array.from(s2_h0, s2_h1, s2_h2, s2_h3, s2_h4, s2_h5)
        array<float> s2l = array.from(s2_l0, s2_l1, s2_l2, s2_l3, s2_l4, s2_l5)
        array<float> s3h = array.from(s3_h0, s3_h1, s3_h2, s3_h3, s3_h4, s3_h5)
        array<float> s3l = array.from(s3_l0, s3_l1, s3_l2, s3_l3, s3_l4, s3_l5)
        bool isSeq = show_ssmt and isSeqTF(tfSecs)

        // The level-break windows are prefix ranges [0, j-1]: they depend on the OLDER anchor j and
        // never on the tip i, so computing them inside the j loop redid the same seven scans for
        // every (i, j) pair. Hoisted to eight running-extreme arrays built once per call and then
        // read by index — identical values, an order of magnitude fewer scans per realtime tick.
        array<float> chH = array.new<float>(size, na)
        array<float> chL = array.new<float>(size, na)
        for q = 0 to size - 1
            Candle cq = candleSet.candles.get(q)
            chH.set(q, cq.h)
            chL.set(q, cq.l)
        array<float> chHiPre = preHi(chH)
        array<float> chLoPre = preLo(chL)
        array<float> s1hPre = preHi(s1h)
        array<float> s1lPre = preLo(s1l)
        array<float> s2hPre = preHi(s2h)
        array<float> s2lPre = preLo(s2l)
        array<float> s3hPre = preHi(s3h)
        array<float> s3lPre = preLo(s3l)

        // Cap the newer-candle index at 4, not 5. The correlated-symbol arrays hold
        // only 6 offsets (0..5) and a pair needs j > i, so the deepest valid newer candle is i=4
        // (pairing with j=5). Allowing i=5 made the inner `for j = i+1 to jMax` become `for j = 6 to
        // 5`, which Pine runs BACKWARDS (start > end), hitting s1h.get(6) → RE10045 out-of-bounds.
        // Capping at 4 loses no pairs (deepest is still C0..C5) and keeps the inner loop forward-only.
        // The loop covers every tip the data allows; div_max_tips gates DRAWING further down, and
        // an SSMT is exempt from it — sequential divergences are the ones worth acting on, so a
        // display filter must not be able to hide one.
        int iMax = math.min(size - 2, 4)
        for i = 0 to iMax
            Candle ci = candleSet.candles.get(i)
            float s1hi = s1h.get(i)
            float s1li = s1l.get(i)
            float s2hi = s2h.get(i)
            float s2li = s2l.get(i)
            float s3hi = s3h.get(i)
            float s3li = s3l.get(i)
            // Per-tip merge accumulators (see DetectDivergence).
            // Within the tip cap? An SSMT overrides this (see iMax comment).
            bool tipOk = i < div_max_tips
            int mLoJ = -1
            int mHiJ = -1
            // Did THIS tip diverge with its immediately preceding candle? Recorded separately from
            // mLoJ/mHiJ because the merge keeps the FURTHEST anchor — without this, widening the
            // drawn span past the adjacent candle would silently drop the SSMT flag, the same way
            // the overlay merge used to hide SMTF behind a higher timeframe.
            bool mLoAdj = false
            bool mHiAdj = false
            bool mLb1 = false
            bool mLb2 = false
            bool mLb3 = false
            bool mHb1 = false
            bool mHb2 = false
            bool mHb3 = false
            int jMax = math.min(math.min(i + div_lookback, size - 1), 5)
            for j = i + 1 to jMax
                Candle cj = candleSet.candles.get(j)

                // Level-break guard, identical to the column detector (per asset): the SMT's
                // extreme must hold over [0, j-1] — a new high/low printed by any candle newer than the tip voids it.
                float chHiMax = chHiPre.get(j - 1)
                float chLoMin = chLoPre.get(j - 1)
                bool chHiOk = na(chHiMax) or chHiMax <= math.max(ci.h, cj.h)
                bool chLoOk = na(chLoMin) or chLoMin >= math.min(ci.l, cj.l)
                float s1HiInt = s1hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s1LoInt = s1lPre.get(j - 1)
                float s2HiInt = s2hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s2LoInt = s2lPre.get(j - 1)
                float s3HiInt = s3hPre.get(j - 1)
                float s3LoInt = s3lPre.get(j - 1)

                bool v1 = psp_sym1_enabled and not na(s1hi) and not na(s1li) and not na(s1h.get(j)) and not na(s1l.get(j))
                bool s1HiOk = na(s1HiInt) or s1HiInt <= math.max(s1hi, s1h.get(j))
                bool s1LoOk = na(s1LoInt) or s1LoInt >= math.min(s1li, s1l.get(j))
                bool bull1 = v1 and chLoOk and s1LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s1li < s1l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s1li > s1l.get(j)))
                bool bear1 = v1 and chHiOk and s1HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s1hi < s1h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s1hi > s1h.get(j)))
                bool v2 = psp_sym2_enabled and not na(s2hi) and not na(s2li) and not na(s2h.get(j)) and not na(s2l.get(j))
                bool s2HiOk = na(s2HiInt) or s2HiInt <= math.max(s2hi, s2h.get(j))
                bool s2LoOk = na(s2LoInt) or s2LoInt >= math.min(s2li, s2l.get(j))
                bool bull2 = v2 and chLoOk and s2LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s2li < s2l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s2li > s2l.get(j)))
                bool bear2 = v2 and chHiOk and s2HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s2hi < s2h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s2hi > s2h.get(j)))
                bool v3 = psp_sym3_enabled and not na(s3hi) and not na(s3li) and not na(s3h.get(j)) and not na(s3l.get(j))
                bool s3HiOk = na(s3HiInt) or s3HiInt <= math.max(s3hi, s3h.get(j))
                bool s3LoOk = na(s3LoInt) or s3LoInt >= math.min(s3li, s3l.get(j))
                bool bull3 = v3 and chLoOk and s3LoOk and ((ci.l >= cj.l and s3li < s3l.get(j)) or (ci.l <= cj.l and s3li > s3l.get(j)))
                bool bear3 = v3 and chHiOk and s3HiOk and ((ci.h >= cj.h and s3hi < s3h.get(j)) or (ci.h <= cj.h and s3hi > s3h.get(j)))
                // ANY vs ALL. With require-all, a symbol that is unticked or has no data (vN false)
                // is skipped, not counted as a failure — otherwise a blank Corr. 3 would silence
                // every SMT on the chart. At least one enabled symbol must still be present.
                bool bullHit = div_require_all ? ((v1 or v2 or v3) and (not v1 or bull1) and (not v2 or bull2) and (not v3 or bull3)) : (bull1 or bull2 or bull3)
                bool bearHit = div_require_all ? ((v1 or v2 or v3) and (not v1 or bear1) and (not v2 or bear2) and (not v3 or bear3)) : (bear1 or bear2 or bear3)

                if div_merge
                    if bullHit
                        mLoJ := j
                        mLb1 := bull1
                        mLb2 := bull2
                        mLb3 := bull3
                        if j == i + 1
                            mLoAdj := true
                    if bearHit
                        mHiJ := j
                        mHb1 := bear1
                        mHb2 := bear2
                        mHb3 := bear3
                        if j == i + 1
                            mHiAdj := true
                else
                    string bull_text = ""
                    if bull1
                        bull_text := psp_sym1_short
                    if bull2
                        bull_text := bull_text == "" ? psp_sym2_short : bull_text + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                    if bull3
                        bull_text := bull_text == "" ? psp_sym3_short : bull_text + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                    string bear_text = ""
                    if bear1
                        bear_text := psp_sym1_short
                    if bear2
                        bear_text := bear_text == "" ? psp_sym2_short : bear_text + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                    if bear3
                        bear_text := bear_text == "" ? psp_sym3_short : bear_text + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                    // Collect rather than draw — the cross-timeframe resolve pass
                    // after all six HTFs decides what actually gets a line.
                    if bullHit and (tipOk or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                        bool sfLo = false
                        if show_smtf
                            sfLo := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.l)
                            if not sfLo and bull1
                                sfLo := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1l.get(i))
                            if not sfLo and bull2
                                sfLo := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2l.get(i))
                            if not sfLo and bull3
                                sfLo := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3l.get(i))
                        array.push(chart_cands, ChartSMTCand.new(false, cj.l_idx, cj.l, ci.l_idx, ci.l, smtPrefix(isSeq and j == i + 1, sfLo) + bull_text + " " + tfName, tfSecs, sfLo, isSeq and j == i + 1))
                    if bearHit and (tipOk or (isSeq and j == i + 1))
                        bool sfHi = false
                        if show_smtf
                            sfHi := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.h)
                            if not sfHi and bear1
                                sfHi := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1h.get(i))
                            if not sfHi and bear2
                                sfHi := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2h.get(i))
                            if not sfHi and bear3
                                sfHi := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3h.get(i))
                        array.push(chart_cands, ChartSMTCand.new(true, cj.h_idx, cj.h, ci.h_idx, ci.h, smtPrefix(isSeq and j == i + 1, sfHi) + bear_text + " " + tfName, tfSecs, sfHi, isSeq and j == i + 1))

            // One merged chart SMT per TIP candle (was one per column), matching
            // the column detector, so a divergence ending on a closed candle stays drawn.
            // collected, not drawn — see the resolve pass after the six HTF calls.
            if div_merge and mLoJ != -1 and (tipOk or (isSeq and mLoAdj))
                Candle cjL = candleSet.candles.get(mLoJ)
                string tL = ""
                if mLb1
                    tL := psp_sym1_short
                if mLb2
                    tL := tL == "" ? psp_sym2_short : tL + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                if mLb3
                    tL := tL == "" ? psp_sym3_short : tL + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                // SMTF — same test the column detector runs, so the overlay label matches its column.
                bool gapL = false
                if show_smtf
                    gapL := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.l)
                    if not gapL and mLb1
                        gapL := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1l.get(i))
                    if not gapL and mLb2
                        gapL := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2l.get(i))
                    if not gapL and mLb3
                        gapL := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3l.get(i))
                tL := smtPrefix(isSeq and mLoAdj, gapL) + tL
                array.push(chart_cands, ChartSMTCand.new(false, cjL.l_idx, cjL.l, ci.l_idx, ci.l, tL + " " + tfName, tfSecs, gapL, isSeq and mLoAdj))
            if div_merge and mHiJ != -1 and (tipOk or (isSeq and mHiAdj))
                Candle cjH = candleSet.candles.get(mHiJ)
                string tH = ""
                if mHb1
                    tH := psp_sym1_short
                if mHb2
                    tH := tH == "" ? psp_sym2_short : tH + " & " + psp_sym2_short
                if mHb3
                    tH := tH == "" ? psp_sym3_short : tH + " & " + psp_sym3_short
                bool gapH = false
                if show_smtf
                    gapH := symInGap(candleSet.hHist, candleSet.lHist, i, ci.h)
                    if not gapH and mHb1
                        gapH := symInGap(s1h, s1l, i, s1h.get(i))
                    if not gapH and mHb2
                        gapH := symInGap(s2h, s2l, i, s2h.get(i))
                    if not gapH and mHb3
                        gapH := symInGap(s3h, s3l, i, s3h.get(i))
                tH := smtPrefix(isSeq and mHiAdj, gapH) + tH
                array.push(chart_cands, ChartSMTCand.new(true, cjH.h_idx, cjH.h, ci.h_idx, ci.h, tH + " " + tfName, tfSecs, gapH, isSeq and mHiAdj))
    candleSet

// Per-symbol strength-switch evaluation. Chart and correlated data both come
// from the bundled security calls (c_* = chart symbol, s-prefix args = correlated symbol),
// so the sweep lookback is independent of how many candles the column displays.
//  d* = candle direction (1 = bull close, 0 = bear close); h*/l* by candle index
//  (0 = forming, 1 = last closed, 2..5 = older closed candles).
// The reference extreme for sweep / failure-to-pair tests is the highest high / lowest low
// of the previous `ss_lookback` candles (1 = adjacent candle only, up to 4 — sweeps of an
// extreme sitting several candles back still register).
// SS-PSP = a PSP where exactly ONE asset takes out the lookback extreme while the other
// fails to pair it. With ss_require_reversal ON, the sweeper must additionally close
// against its sweep (textbook reversal flavor); OFF also admits the catch-up flavor.
// Returns [ss_psp_c1_bull, ss_psp_c1_bear, ss_psp_c0_bull, ss_psp_c0_bear].
// It used to also return a hard-coded (C0,C1) SS-SMT pair. replaced that with
// ssSmtBullPair / ssSmtBearPair, which run on any (tip, anchor) pair, and the two values were left
// in the tuple unread — six "declared but never used" warnings across the three call sites.

// The SS-SMT test, generalised to an ARBITRARY (tip, anchor) candle pair so a
// divergence between two closed candles is evaluated exactly like one ending on the forming
// candle. `t` = tip (newer) index, `a` = anchor (older) index; the order-paired extreme is the
// ss_lookback window immediately older than the anchor. With (t,a) = (0,1) these reproduce the
// consecutive-pair logic ssForSymbol applies to the live pair, so nothing previously tagged is lost.
// Directional, as before: only the asset that swept the extreme may show the momentary strength.
ssSmtBullPair(array<float> cL, array<float> sL, int t, int a) =>
    int frm = a + 1
    int upto = math.min(a + ss_lookback, 5)
    float cPL = arrLo(cL, frm, upto)
    float sPL = arrLo(sL, frm, upto)
    float cLt = cL.get(t)
    float cLa = cL.get(a)
    float sLt = sL.get(t)
    float sLa = sL.get(a)
    bool v = not na(cLt) and not na(cLa) and not na(sLt) and not na(sLa)
    v and ((not na(cPL) and cLa < cPL and cLt > cLa and sLt < sLa) or (not na(sPL) and sLa < sPL and sLt > sLa and cLt < cLa))

ssSmtBearPair(array<float> cH, array<float> sH, int t, int a) =>
    int frm = a + 1
    int upto = math.min(a + ss_lookback, 5)
    float cPH = arrHi(cH, frm, upto)
    float sPH = arrHi(sH, frm, upto)
    float cHt = cH.get(t)
    float cHa = cH.get(a)
    float sHt = sH.get(t)
    float sHa = sH.get(a)
    bool v = not na(cHt) and not na(cHa) and not na(sHt) and not na(sHa)
    v and ((not na(cPH) and cHa > cPH and cHt < cHa and sHt > sHa) or (not na(sPH) and sHa > sPH and sHt < sHa and cHt > cHa))

ssForSymbol(float c_d0, float c_d1, float c_h0, float c_l0, float c_h1, float c_l1, float c_h2, float c_l2, float c_h3, float c_l3, float c_h4, float c_l4, float c_h5, float c_l5,
            float d0, float d1, float h0, float l0, float h1, float l1, float h2, float l2, float h3, float l3, float h4, float l4, float h5, float l5) =>
    bool vc = not na(c_h0) and not na(c_l0) and not na(c_h1) and not na(c_l1) and not na(c_h2) and not na(c_l2) and not na(c_d0) and not na(c_d1)
    bool vs = not na(h0) and not na(l0) and not na(h1) and not na(l1) and not na(h2) and not na(l2) and not na(d0) and not na(d1)

    // Reference extremes over the lookback window, per candle index.
    float cPH1 = hiOf(ss_lookback, c_h2, c_h3, c_h4, c_h5)   // prior high for C1
    float cPL1 = loOf(ss_lookback, c_l2, c_l3, c_l4, c_l5)
    float cPH0 = hiOf(ss_lookback, c_h1, c_h2, c_h3, c_h4)   // prior high for C0
    float cPL0 = loOf(ss_lookback, c_l1, c_l2, c_l3, c_l4)
    float sPH1 = hiOf(ss_lookback, h2, h3, h4, h5)
    float sPL1 = loOf(ss_lookback, l2, l3, l4, l5)
    float sPH0 = hiOf(ss_lookback, h1, h2, h3, h4)
    float sPL0 = loOf(ss_lookback, l1, l2, l3, l4)

    // SS-PSP: PSP (opposite closes) + exactly one asset order-pairs the lookback extreme
    // while the other fails to pair it. Evaluated on C1 (confirmed) and C0 (developing).
    bool psp1 = vc and vs and c_d1 != d1
    bool psp0 = vc and vs and c_d0 != d0
    // Split tests: chart sweeps / symbol fails, or symbol sweeps / chart fails.
    bool split_h1 = (c_h1 > cPH1 and h1 <= sPH1) or (h1 > sPH1 and c_h1 <= cPH1)
    bool split_l1 = (c_l1 < cPL1 and l1 >= sPL1) or (l1 < sPL1 and c_l1 >= cPL1)
    bool split_h0 = (c_h0 > cPH0 and h0 <= sPH0) or (h0 > sPH0 and c_h0 <= cPH0)
    bool split_l0 = (c_l0 < cPL0 and l0 >= sPL0) or (l0 < sPL0 and c_l0 >= cPL0)
    // Optional strict mode: the sweeping asset must close against its sweep.
    bool rev_h1 = not ss_require_reversal or (c_h1 > cPH1 ? c_d1 == 0.0 : d1 == 0.0)
    bool rev_l1 = not ss_require_reversal or (c_l1 < cPL1 ? c_d1 == 1.0 : d1 == 1.0)
    bool rev_h0 = not ss_require_reversal or (c_h0 > cPH0 ? c_d0 == 0.0 : d0 == 0.0)
    bool rev_l0 = not ss_require_reversal or (c_l0 < cPL0 ? c_d0 == 1.0 : d0 == 1.0)

    bool ss_psp_c1_bull = psp1 and split_l1 and rev_l1
    bool ss_psp_c1_bear = psp1 and split_h1 and rev_h1
    bool ss_psp_c0_bull = psp0 and split_l0 and rev_l0
    bool ss_psp_c0_bear = psp0 and split_h0 and rev_h0

    [ss_psp_c1_bull, ss_psp_c1_bear, ss_psp_c0_bull, ss_psp_c0_bear]

// Strength Switch detection — the four "cracks in correlation",
// evaluated per correlated symbol via ssForSymbol and OR-aggregated (any symbol producing
// the formation qualifies, mirroring the PSP "ANY" default).
//  - SS-SMT (one-stage):  directional lookback-pair SMT right after a lookback extreme is
//    order-paired (sweeper shows strength, counterpart continues). applied
//    to every drawn SMT via its stored anchor, not only the newest consecutive pairs.
//  - Two-stage SS-SMT:    + a PSP on the SMT's newer candle; direction-agnostic here.
//  - SS-PSP (one-stage):  PSP + sweep/failure split on the lookback extreme (reversal close
//    optional via the strict toggle).
//  - Two-stage SS-PSP:    the SS-PSP on C1 followed by the consecutive-candle SMT on (C0,C1).
// Stateless visual pass: ApplyPSP / DetectDivergence rebuild their label text every last-bar
// tick before this runs, so the SS / SS² prefixes never accumulate across ticks.
method DetectStrengthSwitch(CandleSet candleSet,
                            float c_d0, float c_d1, float c_d2, float c_h0, float c_l0, float c_h1, float c_l1, float c_h2, float c_l2, float c_h3, float c_l3, float c_h4, float c_l4, float c_h5, float c_l5,
                            float s1_d0, float s1_d1, float s1_d2, float s1_h0, float s1_l0, float s1_h1, float s1_l1, float s1_h2, float s1_l2, float s1_h3, float s1_l3, float s1_h4, float s1_l4, float s1_h5, float s1_l5,
                            float s2_d0, float s2_d1, float s2_d2, float s2_h0, float s2_l0, float s2_h1, float s2_l1, float s2_h2, float s2_l2, float s2_h3, float s2_l3, float s2_h4, float s2_l4, float s2_h5, float s2_l5,
                            float s3_d0, float s3_d1, float s3_d2, float s3_h0, float s3_l0, float s3_h1, float s3_l1, float s3_h2, float s3_l2, float s3_h3, float s3_l3, float s3_h4, float s3_l4, float s3_h5, float s3_l5) =>
    if candleSet.candles.size() >= 2 and barstate.islast
        Candle c0 = candleSet.candles.get(0)
        Candle c1 = candleSet.candles.get(1)

        [psp1_bull_1, psp1_bear_1, psp0_bull_1, psp0_bear_1] = ssForSymbol(c_d0, c_d1, c_h0, c_l0, c_h1, c_l1, c_h2, c_l2, c_h3, c_l3, c_h4, c_l4, c_h5, c_l5, s1_d0, s1_d1, s1_h0, s1_l0, s1_h1, s1_l1, s1_h2, s1_l2, s1_h3, s1_l3, s1_h4, s1_l4, s1_h5, s1_l5)
        [psp1_bull_2, psp1_bear_2, psp0_bull_2, psp0_bear_2] = ssForSymbol(c_d0, c_d1, c_h0, c_l0, c_h1, c_l1, c_h2, c_l2, c_h3, c_l3, c_h4, c_l4, c_h5, c_l5, s2_d0, s2_d1, s2_h0, s2_l0, s2_h1, s2_l1, s2_h2, s2_l2, s2_h3, s2_l3, s2_h4, s2_l4, s2_h5, s2_l5)
        [psp1_bull_3, psp1_bear_3, psp0_bull_3, psp0_bear_3] = ssForSymbol(c_d0, c_d1, c_h0, c_l0, c_h1, c_l1, c_h2, c_l2, c_h3, c_l3, c_h4, c_l4, c_h5, c_l5, s3_d0, s3_d1, s3_h0, s3_l0, s3_h1, s3_l1, s3_h2, s3_l2, s3_h3, s3_l3, s3_h4, s3_l4, s3_h5, s3_l5)

        // Every correlation is gated on its own tick, matching PSP and both divergence detectors.
        // Corr. 3 always was (psp_sym3_enabled); 1 and 2 were not, so an unticked correlation still
        // produced SS tags — the one place in the script where "untick and it is ignored everywhere"
        // was not true. The SS module predates the per-correlation toggles and was extracted before
        // they landed, so it never picked them up.
        bool ss_psp_c1_bull = (psp_sym1_enabled and psp1_bull_1) or (psp_sym2_enabled and psp1_bull_2) or (psp_sym3_enabled and psp1_bull_3)
        bool ss_psp_c1_bear = (psp_sym1_enabled and psp1_bear_1) or (psp_sym2_enabled and psp1_bear_2) or (psp_sym3_enabled and psp1_bear_3)
        bool ss_psp_c0      = (psp_sym1_enabled and (psp0_bull_1 or psp0_bear_1)) or (psp_sym2_enabled and (psp0_bull_2 or psp0_bear_2)) or (psp_sym3_enabled and (psp0_bull_3 or psp0_bear_3))

        // Two-stage SS-PSP: the SS-PSP on C1 followed by the matching-direction SMT on the
        // following (C0,C1) pair — the live evaluation, whose flags live on C0.
        bool ss2_psp = (ss_psp_c1_bull and c0.has_bullish_div) or (ss_psp_c1_bear and c0.has_bearish_div)

        // Tag PSP labels + SS border. C0's SS-PSP can only ever be one-stage — its follow-up
        // SMT would form on the next candle pair, which doesn't exist yet.
        if ss_show_psp and (ss_psp_c1_bull or ss_psp_c1_bear) and (not ss_two_stage_only or ss2_psp)
            box.set_border_color(c1.body, ss_border_color)
            if not na(c1.psp_label)
                c1.psp_label.set_text((ss2_psp ? "SS² " : "SS ") + label.get_text(c1.psp_label))
        // The forming candle's SS-PSP is one-stage by definition, so "two-stage only" hides it.
        if ss_show_psp and ss_psp_c0 and not ss_two_stage_only
            box.set_border_color(c0.body, ss_border_color)
            if not na(c0.psp_label)
                c0.psp_label.set_text("SS " + label.get_text(c0.psp_label))

        // SS-SMT tagging generalised to EVERY drawn column SMT. Each tip candle now
        // carries the label + anchor index DetectDivergence stashed on it, and the sweep test runs
        // on that (tip, anchor) pair via ssSmtBullPair / ssSmtBearPair rather than the hard-coded
        // (C0,C1) pair — so a confirmed divergence between two CLOSED candles is tagged exactly like
        // a live one. Two-stage ("SS²") = a PSP on the SMT's own tip candle. Labels are rebuilt by
        // DetectDivergence every tick, so prefixes never accumulate. Merge mode only.
        // Gated as a whole: with SS-SMT off these eight arrays are never built either, which is
        // most of what this pass costs.
        if ss_show_smt
            array<float> chH = array.from(c_h0, c_h1, c_h2, c_h3, c_h4, c_h5)
            array<float> chL = array.from(c_l0, c_l1, c_l2, c_l3, c_l4, c_l5)
            array<float> a1H = array.from(s1_h0, s1_h1, s1_h2, s1_h3, s1_h4, s1_h5)
            array<float> a1L = array.from(s1_l0, s1_l1, s1_l2, s1_l3, s1_l4, s1_l5)
            array<float> a2H = array.from(s2_h0, s2_h1, s2_h2, s2_h3, s2_h4, s2_h5)
            array<float> a2L = array.from(s2_l0, s2_l1, s2_l2, s2_l3, s2_l4, s2_l5)
            array<float> a3H = array.from(s3_h0, s3_h1, s3_h2, s3_h3, s3_h4, s3_h5)
            array<float> a3L = array.from(s3_l0, s3_l1, s3_l2, s3_l3, s3_l4, s3_l5)
            for ti = 0 to math.min(candleSet.candles.size() - 1, 5)
                Candle ct = candleSet.candles.get(ti)
                // ct.is_psp IS the two-stage condition here: the SMT's own tip candle is a PSP.
                bool twoStageOk = not ss_two_stage_only or ct.is_psp
                if not na(ct.smt_low_lbl) and ct.smt_low_anchor >= 0
                    bool lb1 = psp_sym1_enabled and ssSmtBullPair(chL, a1L, ti, ct.smt_low_anchor)
                    bool lb2 = psp_sym2_enabled and ssSmtBullPair(chL, a2L, ti, ct.smt_low_anchor)
                    bool lb3 = psp_sym3_enabled and ssSmtBullPair(chL, a3L, ti, ct.smt_low_anchor)
                    if (lb1 or lb2 or lb3) and twoStageOk
                        ct.smt_low_lbl.set_text((ct.is_psp ? "SS² " : "SS ") + label.get_text(ct.smt_low_lbl))
                if not na(ct.smt_high_lbl) and ct.smt_high_anchor >= 0
                    bool hb1 = psp_sym1_enabled and ssSmtBearPair(chH, a1H, ti, ct.smt_high_anchor)
                    bool hb2 = psp_sym2_enabled and ssSmtBearPair(chH, a2H, ti, ct.smt_high_anchor)
                    bool hb3 = psp_sym3_enabled and ssSmtBearPair(chH, a3H, ti, ct.smt_high_anchor)
                    if (hb1 or hb2 or hb3) and twoStageOk
                        ct.smt_high_lbl.set_text((ct.is_psp ? "SS² " : "SS ") + label.get_text(ct.smt_high_lbl))
    candleSet

method DetectSwings(CandleSet candleSet) =>
    // Check candles (excluding the most recent at index 0) and create/delete swing lines
    if candleSet.candles.size() >= 2
        // Start from index 1 (skip index 0 which is the most recent/forming candle)
        for i = 1 to candleSet.candles.size() - 1
            Candle this_candle = candleSet.candles.get(i)
            Candle next_candle = candleSet.candles.get(i - 1)  // Next candle (toward index 0 = more recent)
            
            // For deletion logic, check if swing is invalidated
            // For index 1: Don't delete (next candle is forming - potential swing)
            // For index > 1: Delete only if closed candle invalidated (didn't reject)
            
            if i > 1
                // Confirmed swing high: swept with rejection
                bool is_swing_high = next_candle.h > this_candle.h and next_candle.c < this_candle.h
                // Confirmed swing low: swept with rejection
                bool is_swing_low = next_candle.l < this_candle.l and next_candle.c > this_candle.l
                
                // Delete if closed candle failed to reject
                if not is_swing_high and not na(this_candle.swing_high_line)
                    line.delete(this_candle.swing_high_line)
                    this_candle.swing_high_line := na
                
                if not is_swing_low and not na(this_candle.swing_low_line)
                    line.delete(this_candle.swing_low_line)
                    this_candle.swing_low_line := na
            // For i == 1: Don't delete lines (potential swings from forming candle)
            
            // Update the candle in the array
            candleSet.candles.set(i, this_candle)
    
    candleSet

// Populate the per-HTF "visible × valid-timeframe" cache + the HTFEnabled
// count once on barstate.isfirst. The `var` declarations themselves sit with the other globals and
// must precede the methods that read them. All inputs read here are constants for the script run,
// and Pine restarts from bar 0 on any input change, so the cache is always fresh.
if barstate.isfirst
    // `and not qt_quarterly` last: a per-chart-TF visibility slot can otherwise override the main
    // show flag and put the 15m column back while Quarterly is ticked.
    helper.htf1_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(1, htf1.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf1.settings.htf) and not qt_quarterly
    helper.htf2_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(2, htf2.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf2.settings.htf)
    helper.htf3_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(3, htf3.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf3.settings.htf)
    helper.htf4_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(4, htf4.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf4.settings.htf)
    helper.htf5_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(5, htf5.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf5.settings.htf)
    helper.htf6_active := isHTFVisibleOnCurrentTF(6, htf6.settings.show) and helper.ValidTimeframe(htf6.settings.htf)
    helper.htf_enabled_count := helper.HTFEnabled()

// Clear the all-pairs column-SMT pool before the HTF loop repopulates it
// (last bar only; mirrors how chart_divs is managed).
if barstate.islast and array.size(col_smts) > 0
    for smtI = array.size(col_smts) - 1 to 0
        ColumnSMT cs = array.get(col_smts, smtI)
        if not na(cs.ln)
            line.delete(cs.ln)
        if not na(cs.lbl)
            label.delete(cs.lbl)
    array.clear(col_smts)

int cnt = 0
int last = helper.htf_enabled_count

int offset = settings.offset
if helper.htf1_active
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe'
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe' and settings.max_sets == 1
        showTrace := true
    htf1.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf1.Monitor(_new_htf1).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf1.DetectDivergence(offset, psp1_s1_h0, psp1_s1_l0, psp1_s1_h1, psp1_s1_l1, psp1_s1_h2, psp1_s1_l2, psp1_s1_h3, psp1_s1_l3, psp1_s1_h4, psp1_s1_l4, psp1_s1_h5, psp1_s1_l5, psp1_s2_h0, psp1_s2_l0, psp1_s2_h1, psp1_s2_l1, psp1_s2_h2, psp1_s2_l2, psp1_s2_h3, psp1_s2_l3, psp1_s2_h4, psp1_s2_l4, psp1_s2_h5, psp1_s2_l5, psp1_s3_h0, psp1_s3_l0, psp1_s3_h1, psp1_s3_l1, psp1_s3_h2, psp1_s3_l2, psp1_s3_h3, psp1_s3_l3, psp1_s3_h4, psp1_s3_l4, psp1_s3_h5, psp1_s3_l5)
    cnt := cnt + 1
    offset := offset + htf1.candles.size() * settings.width + (htf1.candles.size() > 0 ? (htf1.candles.size() - 1) * settings.buffer : 0) + settings.htf_buffer  // dropped always-true `cnt > 0 ?` outer ternary
if helper.htf2_active and cnt < last
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe' and cnt == 0
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe' and cnt == last - 1
        showTrace := true
    htf2.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf2.Monitor(_new_htf2).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf2.DetectDivergence(offset, psp2_s1_h0, psp2_s1_l0, psp2_s1_h1, psp2_s1_l1, psp2_s1_h2, psp2_s1_l2, psp2_s1_h3, psp2_s1_l3, psp2_s1_h4, psp2_s1_l4, psp2_s1_h5, psp2_s1_l5, psp2_s2_h0, psp2_s2_l0, psp2_s2_h1, psp2_s2_l1, psp2_s2_h2, psp2_s2_l2, psp2_s2_h3, psp2_s2_l3, psp2_s2_h4, psp2_s2_l4, psp2_s2_h5, psp2_s2_l5, psp2_s3_h0, psp2_s3_l0, psp2_s3_h1, psp2_s3_l1, psp2_s3_h2, psp2_s3_l2, psp2_s3_h3, psp2_s3_l3, psp2_s3_h4, psp2_s3_l4, psp2_s3_h5, psp2_s3_l5)
    cnt := cnt + 1
    offset := offset + htf2.candles.size() * settings.width + (htf2.candles.size() > 0 ? (htf2.candles.size() - 1) * settings.buffer : 0) + settings.htf_buffer
if helper.htf3_active and cnt < last
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe' and cnt == 0
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe' and cnt == last - 1
        showTrace := true
    htf3.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf3.Monitor(_new_htf3).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf3.DetectDivergence(offset, psp3_s1_h0, psp3_s1_l0, psp3_s1_h1, psp3_s1_l1, psp3_s1_h2, psp3_s1_l2, psp3_s1_h3, psp3_s1_l3, psp3_s1_h4, psp3_s1_l4, psp3_s1_h5, psp3_s1_l5, psp3_s2_h0, psp3_s2_l0, psp3_s2_h1, psp3_s2_l1, psp3_s2_h2, psp3_s2_l2, psp3_s2_h3, psp3_s2_l3, psp3_s2_h4, psp3_s2_l4, psp3_s2_h5, psp3_s2_l5, psp3_s3_h0, psp3_s3_l0, psp3_s3_h1, psp3_s3_l1, psp3_s3_h2, psp3_s3_l2, psp3_s3_h3, psp3_s3_l3, psp3_s3_h4, psp3_s3_l4, psp3_s3_h5, psp3_s3_l5)
    cnt := cnt + 1
    offset := offset + htf3.candles.size() * settings.width + (htf3.candles.size() > 0 ? (htf3.candles.size() - 1) * settings.buffer : 0) + settings.htf_buffer
if helper.htf4_active and cnt < last
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe' and cnt == 0
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe' and cnt == last - 1
        showTrace := true
    htf4.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf4.Monitor(_new_htf4).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf4.DetectDivergence(offset, psp4_s1_h0, psp4_s1_l0, psp4_s1_h1, psp4_s1_l1, psp4_s1_h2, psp4_s1_l2, psp4_s1_h3, psp4_s1_l3, psp4_s1_h4, psp4_s1_l4, psp4_s1_h5, psp4_s1_l5, psp4_s2_h0, psp4_s2_l0, psp4_s2_h1, psp4_s2_l1, psp4_s2_h2, psp4_s2_l2, psp4_s2_h3, psp4_s2_l3, psp4_s2_h4, psp4_s2_l4, psp4_s2_h5, psp4_s2_l5, psp4_s3_h0, psp4_s3_l0, psp4_s3_h1, psp4_s3_l1, psp4_s3_h2, psp4_s3_l2, psp4_s3_h3, psp4_s3_l3, psp4_s3_h4, psp4_s3_l4, psp4_s3_h5, psp4_s3_l5)
    cnt := cnt + 1
    offset := offset + htf4.candles.size() * settings.width + (htf4.candles.size() > 0 ? (htf4.candles.size() - 1) * settings.buffer : 0) + settings.htf_buffer
if helper.htf5_active and cnt < last
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe' and cnt == 0
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe' and cnt == last - 1
        showTrace := true
    htf5.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf5.Monitor(_new_htf5).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf5.DetectDivergence(offset, psp5_s1_h0, psp5_s1_l0, psp5_s1_h1, psp5_s1_l1, psp5_s1_h2, psp5_s1_l2, psp5_s1_h3, psp5_s1_l3, psp5_s1_h4, psp5_s1_l4, psp5_s1_h5, psp5_s1_l5, psp5_s2_h0, psp5_s2_l0, psp5_s2_h1, psp5_s2_l1, psp5_s2_h2, psp5_s2_l2, psp5_s2_h3, psp5_s2_l3, psp5_s2_h4, psp5_s2_l4, psp5_s2_h5, psp5_s2_l5, psp5_s3_h0, psp5_s3_l0, psp5_s3_h1, psp5_s3_l1, psp5_s3_h2, psp5_s3_l2, psp5_s3_h3, psp5_s3_l3, psp5_s3_h4, psp5_s3_l4, psp5_s3_h5, psp5_s3_l5)
    cnt := cnt + 1
    offset := offset + htf5.candles.size() * settings.width + (htf5.candles.size() > 0 ? (htf5.candles.size() - 1) * settings.buffer : 0) + settings.htf_buffer
if helper.htf6_active and cnt < last
    bool showTrace = false
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'First Timeframe' and cnt == 0
        showTrace := true
    if settings.trace_anchor == 'Last Timeframe'
        showTrace := true
    htf6.UpdateTime(offset)
    htf6.Monitor(_new_htf6).Update(offset, showTrace).FindImbalance().DetectSwings()
    htf6.DetectDivergence(offset, psp6_s1_h0, psp6_s1_l0, psp6_s1_h1, psp6_s1_l1, psp6_s1_h2, psp6_s1_l2, psp6_s1_h3, psp6_s1_l3, psp6_s1_h4, psp6_s1_l4, psp6_s1_h5, psp6_s1_l5, psp6_s2_h0, psp6_s2_l0, psp6_s2_h1, psp6_s2_l1, psp6_s2_h2, psp6_s2_l2, psp6_s2_h3, psp6_s2_l3, psp6_s2_h4, psp6_s2_l4, psp6_s2_h5, psp6_s2_l5, psp6_s3_h0, psp6_s3_l0, psp6_s3_h1, psp6_s3_l1, psp6_s3_h2, psp6_s3_l2, psp6_s3_h3, psp6_s3_l3, psp6_s3_h4, psp6_s3_l4, psp6_s3_h5, psp6_s3_l5)

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- PSP Application (runs on every bar to keep colors & labels current)                                 ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

// Clear last tick's glow before ApplyPSP redraws it — body rings and wick backing both.
if barstate.islast and array.size(psp_glows) > 0
    for gI = array.size(psp_glows) - 1 to 0
        box.delete(array.get(psp_glows, gI))
    array.clear(psp_glows)
if barstate.islast and array.size(psp_glow_wicks) > 0
    for gW = array.size(psp_glow_wicks) - 1 to 0
        line.delete(array.get(psp_glow_wicks, gW))
    array.clear(psp_glow_wicks)

if show_psp and barstate.islast
    if helper.htf1_active
        htf1.ApplyPSP(psp1_s1_d0, psp1_s1_d1, psp1_s1_d2, psp1_s1_d3, psp1_s2_d0, psp1_s2_d1, psp1_s2_d2, psp1_s2_d3, psp1_s3_d0, psp1_s3_d1, psp1_s3_d2, psp1_s3_d3)
    if helper.htf2_active
        htf2.ApplyPSP(psp2_s1_d0, psp2_s1_d1, psp2_s1_d2, psp2_s1_d3, psp2_s2_d0, psp2_s2_d1, psp2_s2_d2, psp2_s2_d3, psp2_s3_d0, psp2_s3_d1, psp2_s3_d2, psp2_s3_d3)
    if helper.htf3_active
        htf3.ApplyPSP(psp3_s1_d0, psp3_s1_d1, psp3_s1_d2, psp3_s1_d3, psp3_s2_d0, psp3_s2_d1, psp3_s2_d2, psp3_s2_d3, psp3_s3_d0, psp3_s3_d1, psp3_s3_d2, psp3_s3_d3)
    if helper.htf4_active
        htf4.ApplyPSP(psp4_s1_d0, psp4_s1_d1, psp4_s1_d2, psp4_s1_d3, psp4_s2_d0, psp4_s2_d1, psp4_s2_d2, psp4_s2_d3, psp4_s3_d0, psp4_s3_d1, psp4_s3_d2, psp4_s3_d3)
    if helper.htf5_active
        htf5.ApplyPSP(psp5_s1_d0, psp5_s1_d1, psp5_s1_d2, psp5_s1_d3, psp5_s2_d0, psp5_s2_d1, psp5_s2_d2, psp5_s2_d3, psp5_s3_d0, psp5_s3_d1, psp5_s3_d2, psp5_s3_d3)
    if helper.htf6_active
        htf6.ApplyPSP(psp6_s1_d0, psp6_s1_d1, psp6_s1_d2, psp6_s1_d3, psp6_s2_d0, psp6_s2_d1, psp6_s2_d2, psp6_s2_d3, psp6_s3_d0, psp6_s3_d1, psp6_s3_d2, psp6_s3_d3)

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Strength Switch Application                                                             ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
// Must run after ApplyPSP (is_psp) and the main flow (divergence flags) so both are fresh
// this tick. With Show PSP Highlights off, is_psp stays false and only SS-SMT can fire.

if show_ss and barstate.islast
    if helper.htf1_active
        htf1.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht1_d0, cht1_d1, cht1_d2, cht1_h0, cht1_l0, cht1_h1, cht1_l1, cht1_h2, cht1_l2, cht1_h3, cht1_l3, cht1_h4, cht1_l4, cht1_h5, cht1_l5, psp1_s1_d0, psp1_s1_d1, psp1_s1_d2, psp1_s1_h0, psp1_s1_l0, psp1_s1_h1, psp1_s1_l1, psp1_s1_h2, psp1_s1_l2, psp1_s1_h3, psp1_s1_l3, psp1_s1_h4, psp1_s1_l4, psp1_s1_h5, psp1_s1_l5, psp1_s2_d0, psp1_s2_d1, psp1_s2_d2, psp1_s2_h0, psp1_s2_l0, psp1_s2_h1, psp1_s2_l1, psp1_s2_h2, psp1_s2_l2, psp1_s2_h3, psp1_s2_l3, psp1_s2_h4, psp1_s2_l4, psp1_s2_h5, psp1_s2_l5, psp1_s3_d0, psp1_s3_d1, psp1_s3_d2, psp1_s3_h0, psp1_s3_l0, psp1_s3_h1, psp1_s3_l1, psp1_s3_h2, psp1_s3_l2, psp1_s3_h3, psp1_s3_l3, psp1_s3_h4, psp1_s3_l4, psp1_s3_h5, psp1_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf2_active
        htf2.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht2_d0, cht2_d1, cht2_d2, cht2_h0, cht2_l0, cht2_h1, cht2_l1, cht2_h2, cht2_l2, cht2_h3, cht2_l3, cht2_h4, cht2_l4, cht2_h5, cht2_l5, psp2_s1_d0, psp2_s1_d1, psp2_s1_d2, psp2_s1_h0, psp2_s1_l0, psp2_s1_h1, psp2_s1_l1, psp2_s1_h2, psp2_s1_l2, psp2_s1_h3, psp2_s1_l3, psp2_s1_h4, psp2_s1_l4, psp2_s1_h5, psp2_s1_l5, psp2_s2_d0, psp2_s2_d1, psp2_s2_d2, psp2_s2_h0, psp2_s2_l0, psp2_s2_h1, psp2_s2_l1, psp2_s2_h2, psp2_s2_l2, psp2_s2_h3, psp2_s2_l3, psp2_s2_h4, psp2_s2_l4, psp2_s2_h5, psp2_s2_l5, psp2_s3_d0, psp2_s3_d1, psp2_s3_d2, psp2_s3_h0, psp2_s3_l0, psp2_s3_h1, psp2_s3_l1, psp2_s3_h2, psp2_s3_l2, psp2_s3_h3, psp2_s3_l3, psp2_s3_h4, psp2_s3_l4, psp2_s3_h5, psp2_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf3_active
        htf3.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht3_d0, cht3_d1, cht3_d2, cht3_h0, cht3_l0, cht3_h1, cht3_l1, cht3_h2, cht3_l2, cht3_h3, cht3_l3, cht3_h4, cht3_l4, cht3_h5, cht3_l5, psp3_s1_d0, psp3_s1_d1, psp3_s1_d2, psp3_s1_h0, psp3_s1_l0, psp3_s1_h1, psp3_s1_l1, psp3_s1_h2, psp3_s1_l2, psp3_s1_h3, psp3_s1_l3, psp3_s1_h4, psp3_s1_l4, psp3_s1_h5, psp3_s1_l5, psp3_s2_d0, psp3_s2_d1, psp3_s2_d2, psp3_s2_h0, psp3_s2_l0, psp3_s2_h1, psp3_s2_l1, psp3_s2_h2, psp3_s2_l2, psp3_s2_h3, psp3_s2_l3, psp3_s2_h4, psp3_s2_l4, psp3_s2_h5, psp3_s2_l5, psp3_s3_d0, psp3_s3_d1, psp3_s3_d2, psp3_s3_h0, psp3_s3_l0, psp3_s3_h1, psp3_s3_l1, psp3_s3_h2, psp3_s3_l2, psp3_s3_h3, psp3_s3_l3, psp3_s3_h4, psp3_s3_l4, psp3_s3_h5, psp3_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf4_active
        htf4.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht4_d0, cht4_d1, cht4_d2, cht4_h0, cht4_l0, cht4_h1, cht4_l1, cht4_h2, cht4_l2, cht4_h3, cht4_l3, cht4_h4, cht4_l4, cht4_h5, cht4_l5, psp4_s1_d0, psp4_s1_d1, psp4_s1_d2, psp4_s1_h0, psp4_s1_l0, psp4_s1_h1, psp4_s1_l1, psp4_s1_h2, psp4_s1_l2, psp4_s1_h3, psp4_s1_l3, psp4_s1_h4, psp4_s1_l4, psp4_s1_h5, psp4_s1_l5, psp4_s2_d0, psp4_s2_d1, psp4_s2_d2, psp4_s2_h0, psp4_s2_l0, psp4_s2_h1, psp4_s2_l1, psp4_s2_h2, psp4_s2_l2, psp4_s2_h3, psp4_s2_l3, psp4_s2_h4, psp4_s2_l4, psp4_s2_h5, psp4_s2_l5, psp4_s3_d0, psp4_s3_d1, psp4_s3_d2, psp4_s3_h0, psp4_s3_l0, psp4_s3_h1, psp4_s3_l1, psp4_s3_h2, psp4_s3_l2, psp4_s3_h3, psp4_s3_l3, psp4_s3_h4, psp4_s3_l4, psp4_s3_h5, psp4_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf5_active
        htf5.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht5_d0, cht5_d1, cht5_d2, cht5_h0, cht5_l0, cht5_h1, cht5_l1, cht5_h2, cht5_l2, cht5_h3, cht5_l3, cht5_h4, cht5_l4, cht5_h5, cht5_l5, psp5_s1_d0, psp5_s1_d1, psp5_s1_d2, psp5_s1_h0, psp5_s1_l0, psp5_s1_h1, psp5_s1_l1, psp5_s1_h2, psp5_s1_l2, psp5_s1_h3, psp5_s1_l3, psp5_s1_h4, psp5_s1_l4, psp5_s1_h5, psp5_s1_l5, psp5_s2_d0, psp5_s2_d1, psp5_s2_d2, psp5_s2_h0, psp5_s2_l0, psp5_s2_h1, psp5_s2_l1, psp5_s2_h2, psp5_s2_l2, psp5_s2_h3, psp5_s2_l3, psp5_s2_h4, psp5_s2_l4, psp5_s2_h5, psp5_s2_l5, psp5_s3_d0, psp5_s3_d1, psp5_s3_d2, psp5_s3_h0, psp5_s3_l0, psp5_s3_h1, psp5_s3_l1, psp5_s3_h2, psp5_s3_l2, psp5_s3_h3, psp5_s3_l3, psp5_s3_h4, psp5_s3_l4, psp5_s3_h5, psp5_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf6_active
        htf6.DetectStrengthSwitch(cht6_d0, cht6_d1, cht6_d2, cht6_h0, cht6_l0, cht6_h1, cht6_l1, cht6_h2, cht6_l2, cht6_h3, cht6_l3, cht6_h4, cht6_l4, cht6_h5, cht6_l5, psp6_s1_d0, psp6_s1_d1, psp6_s1_d2, psp6_s1_h0, psp6_s1_l0, psp6_s1_h1, psp6_s1_l1, psp6_s1_h2, psp6_s1_l2, psp6_s1_h3, psp6_s1_l3, psp6_s1_h4, psp6_s1_l4, psp6_s1_h5, psp6_s1_l5, psp6_s2_d0, psp6_s2_d1, psp6_s2_d2, psp6_s2_h0, psp6_s2_l0, psp6_s2_h1, psp6_s2_l1, psp6_s2_h2, psp6_s2_l2, psp6_s2_h3, psp6_s2_l3, psp6_s2_h4, psp6_s2_l4, psp6_s2_h5, psp6_s2_l5, psp6_s3_d0, psp6_s3_d1, psp6_s3_d2, psp6_s3_h0, psp6_s3_l0, psp6_s3_h1, psp6_s3_l1, psp6_s3_h2, psp6_s3_l2, psp6_s3_h3, psp6_s3_l3, psp6_s3_h4, psp6_s3_l4, psp6_s3_h5, psp6_s3_l5)

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- Chart Divergence Lines                                                                               ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

// Trigger chart-divergence whenever auto-correlation is active OR the legacy Pair-based correlated_symbol is set.
bool _chart_div_active = _psp_auto_active or correlated_symbol != ""

if show_divergence_on_chart and _chart_div_active and barstate.islast
    // Clear all old divergence lines/labels every bar so the overlay updates in real time.
    if array.size(chart_divs) > 0
        for i = array.size(chart_divs) - 1 to 0
            ChartDivergence div = array.get(chart_divs, i)
            if not na(div.high_line)
                line.delete(div.high_line)
            if not na(div.low_line)
                line.delete(div.low_line)
            if not na(div.high_label)
                label.delete(div.high_label)
            if not na(div.low_label)
                label.delete(div.low_label)
        array.clear(chart_divs)
    array.clear(chart_cands)  // rebuild the candidate pool each last-bar tick

    // Every active HTF reports its overlay candidates; the resolve pass below decides what draws.
    if helper.htf1_active
        htf1.DetectChartDivergence(psp1_s1_h0, psp1_s1_l0, psp1_s1_h1, psp1_s1_l1, psp1_s1_h2, psp1_s1_l2, psp1_s1_h3, psp1_s1_l3, psp1_s1_h4, psp1_s1_l4, psp1_s1_h5, psp1_s1_l5, psp1_s2_h0, psp1_s2_l0, psp1_s2_h1, psp1_s2_l1, psp1_s2_h2, psp1_s2_l2, psp1_s2_h3, psp1_s2_l3, psp1_s2_h4, psp1_s2_l4, psp1_s2_h5, psp1_s2_l5, psp1_s3_h0, psp1_s3_l0, psp1_s3_h1, psp1_s3_l1, psp1_s3_h2, psp1_s3_l2, psp1_s3_h3, psp1_s3_l3, psp1_s3_h4, psp1_s3_l4, psp1_s3_h5, psp1_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf2_active
        htf2.DetectChartDivergence(psp2_s1_h0, psp2_s1_l0, psp2_s1_h1, psp2_s1_l1, psp2_s1_h2, psp2_s1_l2, psp2_s1_h3, psp2_s1_l3, psp2_s1_h4, psp2_s1_l4, psp2_s1_h5, psp2_s1_l5, psp2_s2_h0, psp2_s2_l0, psp2_s2_h1, psp2_s2_l1, psp2_s2_h2, psp2_s2_l2, psp2_s2_h3, psp2_s2_l3, psp2_s2_h4, psp2_s2_l4, psp2_s2_h5, psp2_s2_l5, psp2_s3_h0, psp2_s3_l0, psp2_s3_h1, psp2_s3_l1, psp2_s3_h2, psp2_s3_l2, psp2_s3_h3, psp2_s3_l3, psp2_s3_h4, psp2_s3_l4, psp2_s3_h5, psp2_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf3_active
        htf3.DetectChartDivergence(psp3_s1_h0, psp3_s1_l0, psp3_s1_h1, psp3_s1_l1, psp3_s1_h2, psp3_s1_l2, psp3_s1_h3, psp3_s1_l3, psp3_s1_h4, psp3_s1_l4, psp3_s1_h5, psp3_s1_l5, psp3_s2_h0, psp3_s2_l0, psp3_s2_h1, psp3_s2_l1, psp3_s2_h2, psp3_s2_l2, psp3_s2_h3, psp3_s2_l3, psp3_s2_h4, psp3_s2_l4, psp3_s2_h5, psp3_s2_l5, psp3_s3_h0, psp3_s3_l0, psp3_s3_h1, psp3_s3_l1, psp3_s3_h2, psp3_s3_l2, psp3_s3_h3, psp3_s3_l3, psp3_s3_h4, psp3_s3_l4, psp3_s3_h5, psp3_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf4_active
        htf4.DetectChartDivergence(psp4_s1_h0, psp4_s1_l0, psp4_s1_h1, psp4_s1_l1, psp4_s1_h2, psp4_s1_l2, psp4_s1_h3, psp4_s1_l3, psp4_s1_h4, psp4_s1_l4, psp4_s1_h5, psp4_s1_l5, psp4_s2_h0, psp4_s2_l0, psp4_s2_h1, psp4_s2_l1, psp4_s2_h2, psp4_s2_l2, psp4_s2_h3, psp4_s2_l3, psp4_s2_h4, psp4_s2_l4, psp4_s2_h5, psp4_s2_l5, psp4_s3_h0, psp4_s3_l0, psp4_s3_h1, psp4_s3_l1, psp4_s3_h2, psp4_s3_l2, psp4_s3_h3, psp4_s3_l3, psp4_s3_h4, psp4_s3_l4, psp4_s3_h5, psp4_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf5_active
        htf5.DetectChartDivergence(psp5_s1_h0, psp5_s1_l0, psp5_s1_h1, psp5_s1_l1, psp5_s1_h2, psp5_s1_l2, psp5_s1_h3, psp5_s1_l3, psp5_s1_h4, psp5_s1_l4, psp5_s1_h5, psp5_s1_l5, psp5_s2_h0, psp5_s2_l0, psp5_s2_h1, psp5_s2_l1, psp5_s2_h2, psp5_s2_l2, psp5_s2_h3, psp5_s2_l3, psp5_s2_h4, psp5_s2_l4, psp5_s2_h5, psp5_s2_l5, psp5_s3_h0, psp5_s3_l0, psp5_s3_h1, psp5_s3_l1, psp5_s3_h2, psp5_s3_l2, psp5_s3_h3, psp5_s3_l3, psp5_s3_h4, psp5_s3_l4, psp5_s3_h5, psp5_s3_l5)
    if helper.htf6_active
        htf6.DetectChartDivergence(psp6_s1_h0, psp6_s1_l0, psp6_s1_h1, psp6_s1_l1, psp6_s1_h2, psp6_s1_l2, psp6_s1_h3, psp6_s1_l3, psp6_s1_h4, psp6_s1_l4, psp6_s1_h5, psp6_s1_l5, psp6_s2_h0, psp6_s2_l0, psp6_s2_h1, psp6_s2_l1, psp6_s2_h2, psp6_s2_l2, psp6_s2_h3, psp6_s2_l3, psp6_s2_h4, psp6_s2_l4, psp6_s2_h5, psp6_s2_l5, psp6_s3_h0, psp6_s3_l0, psp6_s3_h1, psp6_s3_l1, psp6_s3_h2, psp6_s3_l2, psp6_s3_h3, psp6_s3_l3, psp6_s3_h4, psp6_s3_l4, psp6_s3_h5, psp6_s3_l5)

    // Resolve the collected candidates into actual lines. Precedence is highest
    // timeframe first, then widest span. A candidate is skipped when its bar-index range overlaps
    // one already kept on the SAME side (high/low), so a 15m, 30m and 1H divergence sitting on the
    // same swing collapse to the 1H line instead of stacking three near-identical lines on price.
    // With "Merge overlapping chart SMTs" off, every candidate is drawn (an earlier behaviour).
    // Columns are untouched — they are one timeframe each, so they cannot overlap.
    int nCand = array.size(chart_cands)
    if nCand > 0
        array<bool> taken = array.new<bool>(nCand, false)
        array<int> kHiA = array.new<int>()
        array<int> kHiB = array.new<int>()
        array<int> kLoA = array.new<int>()
        array<int> kLoB = array.new<int>()
        for _n = 0 to nCand - 1
            // Pick the highest-precedence candidate not yet handled (selection sort; nCand is small)
            int best = -1
            for c = 0 to nCand - 1
                if not array.get(taken, c)
                    if best == -1
                        best := c
                    else
                        ChartSMTCand ca = array.get(chart_cands, c)
                        ChartSMTCand cb = array.get(chart_cands, best)
                        // Quality outranks timeframe: SSMTF (3) > SSMT (2) > SMTF (1) > plain (0),
                        // and only then highest timeframe, then widest span. Without this a plain
                        // higher-timeframe SMT covering the same swing suppresses a sequential one
                        // and the flag never reaches the chart while the column still shows it.
                        // Sequential ranks above gap because time is the master filter.
                        int rankA = (ca.isSsmt ? 2 : 0) + (ca.isSmtf ? 1 : 0)
                        int rankB = (cb.isSsmt ? 2 : 0) + (cb.isSmtf ? 1 : 0)
                        if rankA > rankB or (rankA == rankB and (ca.tfSecs > cb.tfSecs or (ca.tfSecs == cb.tfSecs and (ca.xNew - ca.xOld) > (cb.xNew - cb.xOld))))
                            best := c
            if best >= 0
                array.set(taken, best, true)
                ChartSMTCand cd = array.get(chart_cands, best)
                bool clash = false
                if div_chart_merge
                    if cd.isHigh and array.size(kHiA) > 0
                        for q = 0 to array.size(kHiA) - 1
                            if cd.xOld <= array.get(kHiB, q) and array.get(kHiA, q) <= cd.xNew
                                clash := true
                    if not cd.isHigh and array.size(kLoA) > 0
                        for q = 0 to array.size(kLoA) - 1
                            if cd.xOld <= array.get(kLoB, q) and array.get(kLoA, q) <= cd.xNew
                                clash := true
                if not clash
                    if cd.isHigh
                        array.push(kHiA, cd.xOld)
                        array.push(kHiB, cd.xNew)
                    else
                        array.push(kLoA, cd.xOld)
                        array.push(kLoB, cd.xNew)
                    ChartDivergence div = ChartDivergence.new()
                    int midX = math.round((cd.xOld + cd.xNew) / 2.0)
                    float midY = (cd.yOld + cd.yNew) / 2
                    if cd.isHigh
                        div.high_line := line.new(cd.xOld, cd.yOld, cd.xNew, cd.yNew, color=div_high_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                        if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or cd.isSmtf or cd.isSsmt)
                            div.high_label := label.new(midX, midY, cd.txt, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                    else
                        div.low_line := line.new(cd.xOld, cd.yOld, cd.xNew, cd.yNew, color=div_low_color, width=div_line_width, style=div_line_style_value)
                        if div_label_show and (not div_label_smtf_only or cd.isSmtf or cd.isSsmt)
                            div.low_label := label.new(midX, midY, cd.txt, color=color_transparent, textcolor=div_label_color, style=label.style_none, size=div_label_size, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
                    array.push(chart_divs, div)

//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//
//+--- HTF Info Table                                                                                       ---+//
//+------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+//

if show_htf_table and barstate.islast
    // Calculate number of active HTFs
    array<CandleSet> active_htfs = array.new<CandleSet>()
    if helper.htf1_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf1)
    if helper.htf2_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf2)
    if helper.htf3_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf3)
    if helper.htf4_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf4)
    if helper.htf5_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf5)
    if helper.htf6_active
        array.push(active_htfs, htf6)
    
    // Calculate rows: 1 header + enabled data rows
    int num_data_rows = 0
    if show_timer_row
        num_data_rows += 1
    if show_swing_row
        num_data_rows += 1
    if show_expansion_row
        num_data_rows += 1
    if show_divergence_row
        num_data_rows += 1
    
    int num_cols = array.size(active_htfs) + 1  //+1 for row label column
    int num_rows = num_data_rows + (show_timeframe_row ? 1 : 0)  //+1 for timeframe header row
    
    var table htf_info_table = table.new(table_position_value, columns=num_cols, rows=num_rows, border_width=1, frame_width=1)
    
    // Use custom table colors from settings
    color header_bg = table_header_bg
    color header_text = table_header_text
    color label_bg = table_label_bg
    color label_text = table_label_text
    color data_bg = table_cell_bg
    color data_text = table_cell_text
    
    // Populate table
    if num_cols > 1 and num_rows > 0
        int row = 0
        
        // Header row - Timeframes
        if show_timeframe_row
            table.cell(htf_info_table, 0, row, "", bgcolor=header_bg, text_color=header_text, text_size=table_size_value)
            for col = 0 to array.size(active_htfs) - 1
                CandleSet htf = array.get(active_htfs, col)
                string tf_name = helper.HTFName(htf.settings.htf)
                table.cell(htf_info_table, col + 1, row, tf_name, bgcolor=header_bg, text_color=header_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            row += 1
        
        // Time to close row
        if show_timer_row
            table.cell(htf_info_table, 0, row, "Time", bgcolor=label_bg, text_color=label_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            for col = 0 to array.size(active_htfs) - 1
                CandleSet htf = array.get(active_htfs, col)
                string timer = helper.RemainingTime(htf.settings.htf)
                table.cell(htf_info_table, col + 1, row, timer, bgcolor=data_bg, text_color=data_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            row += 1
        
        // Active swing row
        if show_swing_row
            table.cell(htf_info_table, 0, row, "Swing", bgcolor=label_bg, text_color=label_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            for col = 0 to array.size(active_htfs) - 1
                CandleSet htf = array.get(active_htfs, col)
                if htf.candles.size() >= 2
                    Candle c1 = htf.candles.get(0)
                    Candle c2 = htf.candles.get(1)
                    
                    // Check for swing high
                    bool high_broken = c1.h > c2.h
                    bool close_rejected_high = c1.c < c2.h
                    bool confirmed_swing_high = high_broken and close_rejected_high
                    bool potential_swing_high = high_broken and not close_rejected_high
                    
                    // Check for swing low
                    bool low_broken = c1.l < c2.l
                    bool close_rejected_low = c1.c > c2.l
                    bool confirmed_swing_low = low_broken and close_rejected_low
                    bool potential_swing_low = low_broken and not close_rejected_low
                    
                    // Build text with outlined/filled triangles
                    string swing_text = "-"
                    if (confirmed_swing_high or potential_swing_high) and (confirmed_swing_low or potential_swing_low)
                        string high_icon = confirmed_swing_high ? "▼" : "▽"
                        string low_icon = confirmed_swing_low ? "▲" : "△"
                        swing_text := low_icon + high_icon
                    else if confirmed_swing_high
                        swing_text := "▼"
                    else if potential_swing_high
                        swing_text := "▽"
                    else if confirmed_swing_low
                        swing_text := "▲"
                    else if potential_swing_low
                        swing_text := "△"
                    
                    color swing_bg = (confirmed_swing_high or potential_swing_high) and (confirmed_swing_low or potential_swing_low) ? both_swing_color : (confirmed_swing_high or potential_swing_high) ? bearish_swing_color : (confirmed_swing_low or potential_swing_low) ? bullish_swing_color : data_bg
                    table.cell(htf_info_table, col + 1, row, swing_text, bgcolor=swing_bg, text_color=data_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            row += 1
        
        // Expansion row
        if show_expansion_row
            table.cell(htf_info_table, 0, row, "Expand", bgcolor=label_bg, text_color=label_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            for col = 0 to array.size(active_htfs) - 1
                CandleSet htf = array.get(active_htfs, col)
                if htf.candles.size() >= 3
                    Candle c3 = htf.candles.get(0)
                    Candle c2 = htf.candles.get(1)
                    Candle c1 = htf.candles.get(2)
                    bool c2_swing_high = c2.h > c1.h and c2.c < c1.h
                    bool c2_swing_low = c2.l < c1.l and c2.c > c1.l
                    string exp_text = c2_swing_high and c2_swing_low ? "▲▼" : c2_swing_low ? "▲" : c2_swing_high ? "▼" : "-"
                    color exp_bg = c2_swing_high and c2_swing_low ? both_swing_color : c2_swing_low ? bullish_swing_color : c2_swing_high ? bearish_swing_color : data_bg
                    table.cell(htf_info_table, col + 1, row, exp_text, bgcolor=exp_bg, text_color=data_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            row += 1
        
        // Divergence row
        if show_divergence_row
            table.cell(htf_info_table, 0, row, "Divergence", bgcolor=label_bg, text_color=label_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            for col = 0 to array.size(active_htfs) - 1
                CandleSet htf = array.get(active_htfs, col)
                if htf.candles.size() >= 2
                    Candle c2 = htf.candles.get(0)  // live SMT flags are owned by the forming candle
                    bool has_bearish = c2.has_bearish_div
                    bool has_bullish = c2.has_bullish_div
                    string div_text = has_bearish and has_bullish ? "▲▼" : has_bearish ? "▼" : has_bullish ? "▲" : "-"
                    color div_bg = has_bearish and has_bullish ? both_swing_color : has_bearish ? bearish_swing_color : has_bullish ? bullish_swing_color : data_bg
                    table.cell(htf_info_table, col + 1, row, div_text, bgcolor=div_bg, text_color=data_text, text_size=table_size_value, text_font_family=font.family_monospace)
            row += 1
